- @meet_candidates: Meet the eleven candidates

@meet_candidates
title: Eleven candidates, seven electoral fields
on-arrival: pres_candidate_tour_seen = 1

Only the two strongest candidates will advance to the runoff. Lewica's nominee
begins outside those leading positions, but the first round still matters: a
credible result can establish the Left as an independent force, push its issues
into the national campaign and determine what either finalist must offer to
win over its voters.

Before choosing our strategy, we should examine the candidates and the
electorates each hopes to mobilise.

- @candidate_duda: First, the incumbent

@candidate_duda
title: Andrzej Duda — the incumbent
face-image: img/poland/events/pres-candidate-duda-2020.webp

**Andrzej Duda — President of Poland, backed by PiS and the United Right**

PiS presents Duda as the guarantor of continuity: social transfers,
conservative institutions and a presidency working in step with the
government. He begins with the largest disciplined electorate and the full
machinery of the governing camp behind him.

His danger is that the election becomes a verdict on the government's handling
of the pandemic and its failed attempt to force through the May vote.

- @candidate_trzaskowski: KO changed its candidate
- @candidate_kidawa: KO kept its candidate

@candidate_trzaskowski
title: Rafał Trzaskowski — the late challenger
view-if: pres_2020_ko_kidawa = 0
face-image: img/poland/events/pres-candidate-trzaskowski.webp

**Rafał Trzaskowski — Warsaw mayor and KO's replacement candidate**

After Małgorzata Kidawa-Błońska withdraws, Warsaw's mayor enters a shortened
campaign and rapidly rebuilds KO's liberal and metropolitan electorate. He
offers opposition voters a direct institutional challenge to PiS rather than
another attempt to escape the two-bloc contest.

A Trzaskowski victory would place an opposition president above a PiS cabinet.
Vetoes, judicial appointments and the constitutional limits of cohabitation
would become the next political battlefield.

- @candidate_holownia: Now the outsider

@candidate_kidawa
title: Małgorzata Kidawa-Błońska — the candidate KO could not replace
view-if: pres_2020_ko_kidawa = 1
face-image: img/poland/events/pres-candidate-kidawa-2020.webp

**Małgorzata Kidawa-Błońska — KO's primary winner and Deputy Marshal of the
Sejm**

She won the nomination, called for a boycott of a vote that never took place,
and spent the collapse of the calendar losing the argument about whether her
own campaign should continue. It continues anyway. KO's executive could not
agree on a replacement in time, and the mayors who wanted one were told that
overturning a primary in June would cost more than losing with its winner.

She is polling in single figures, which makes the largest anti-PiS electorate
in the country politically homeless for the next six weeks. Where those voters
go — to Hołownia, to us, to the countryside, or nowhere at all — decides who
faces Duda in July.

- @candidate_holownia: Now the outsider

@candidate_holownia
title: Szymon Hołownia — the outsider
face-image: img/poland/events/pres-candidate-holownia-2020.webp

**Szymon Hołownia — independent publicist and television presenter**

Hołownia asks voters exhausted by the PiS–KO conflict to leave both established
camps behind. His campaign combines moderate social language, institutional
reform and a volunteer organisation without an existing parliamentary party.

Even if he misses the runoff, those volunteers and voters may become the basis
of a durable new centrist movement.

- @candidate_bosak: Konfederacja has made its choice

@candidate_bosak
title: Krzysztof Bosak — the radical-right organiser
face-image: img/poland/events/pres-candidate-bosak.webp

**Krzysztof Bosak — Konfederacja MP and National Movement organiser**

Bosak gives Konfederacja a disciplined campaign capable of holding together
nationalists, cultural conservatives and parts of the libertarian right. He
competes with PiS for young men and anti-establishment voters without fully
subordinating his campaign to the governing camp.

His result will determine how seriously either runoff candidate must bargain
for the radical right's endorsement—or its neutrality.

- @candidate_kosiniak: PSL remains in the field

@candidate_kosiniak
title: Władysław Kosiniak-Kamysz — the local moderate
face-image: img/poland/events/pres-candidate-kosiniak-2020.webp

**Władysław Kosiniak-Kamysz — PSL chair and former labour minister**

Kosiniak-Kamysz enters with mayors, county organisations and a rural electorate
that larger parties often remember only during campaigns. He offers a moderate,
institutional candidacy grounded in PSL's local networks.

That space is disappearing around him. Duda dominates much of the countryside,
while Hołownia competes for centrist voters looking beyond the established
parties.

- @candidate_other: The smaller committees have registered too

@candidate_other
title: The smaller committees

Five further candidates complete the eleven-name ballot.


**Stanisław Żółtek**, a veteran of the Congress of the New Right, represents
the libertarian and anti-tax fringe.

**Marek Jakubiak**, businessman and leader of the Federation for the Republic,
appeals to nationalist, entrepreneurial and anti-establishment voters.

**Paweł Tanajno**, an independent entrepreneur, turns the anger of small
business owners and opponents of the lockdown restrictions into an outsider
campaign.

**Waldemar Witkowski**, a housing-cooperative manager and Labour Union
politician, offers a small but recognisably social-democratic alternative.

**Mirosław Piotrowski**, an academic standing for the Movement of True Europe,
represents the hardline Catholic-conservative fringe.

None is likely to threaten the leading candidates. Together, however, they draw
support from several constituencies that might otherwise flow toward the larger
campaigns. In a close runoff, their voters' second choices—or their refusal to
choose—may still affect the result.

- @candidate_left: And our own nominee?

@candidate_left
title: [+ presidential_candidate +] — the Left's nominee

**[+ presidential_candidate +] — Lewica's nominee**
[? if presidential_candidate = "Robert Biedroń": Wiosna's founder and an MEP
offers a media-facing progressive campaign.?][? if presidential_candidate =
"Adrian Zandberg": Razem's co-founder and a Sejm deputy offers a
redistributive campaign built around work and public services.?][? if
presidential_candidate = "Agnieszka Dziemianowicz-Bąk": A Sejm deputy with an
education and social-policy profile offers a bridge between labour and younger
progressives.?][? if presidential_candidate = "Anna-Maria Żukowska": An SLD
spokeswoman and Sejm deputy offers a combative media campaign.?][? if
presidential_candidate = "Katarzyna Kotula": A Wiosna MP and equality
campaigner offers a movement-facing progressive campaign.?][? if
presidential_candidate = "Magdalena Biejat": A Razem Sejm deputy identified
with housing and social policy offers an organiser-led campaign.?]

<div class="face-figure left-candidate-portrait" data-candidate-quality="presidential_candidate"><img class="face-img" alt="Portrait of the Left's presidential nominee"></div>

Our candidate begins outside the runoff places. The campaign can still defend
an independent electorate, force social issues into the contest and determine
which finalist receives Left votes—and at what price.

- @candidate_alignment: Choose the Left's electoral strategy

@candidate_alignment
title: The Left chooses its line

**The field is now complete. Lewica must choose its electoral line.**

With the field mapped, the alliance must decide whether to measure its own
strength or attempt an exceptional common candidacy.

- @separate_candidate
- @joint_request

@separate_candidate
title: Fight under the Left's own colours
subtitle: Keep a distinct candidacy and let every democratic committee test its strength.
on-arrival: {!
Q.pres_ko_joint_candidate = 0;
Q.pres_ko_joint_conversion = 0;
Q.pres_first_calc_mode = "opening_poll";
Q.news_headline =
    Q.presidential_candidate + " begins an independent first-round campaign";
!}
go-to: opening_poll

@joint_request
title: Ask KO to withdraw and back one democratic-social candidate
subtitle: Exceptional path: strong polls, trust, unity and a credible relationship are all required.
choose-if: resources >= 1 and ko_relation >= 60 and left_vote_intent >= 13 and public_trust >= 50 and party_unity >= 60 and (primary_mandate >= 28 or (presidential_candidate = "Robert Biedroń" and spring_dissent <= 15))
unavailable-subtitle: The Left lacks the leverage or legitimacy to turn KO's nomination crisis into a common ticket.
go-to: joint_terms

@joint_terms
title: The price of one democratic candidacy
new-page: true

KO will stand down only for a pact it can defend to its own voters. The choice
sets both the transfer rate and the debts carried into a possible runoff.

- @joint_social
- @joint_institutional
- @separate_candidate: End the talks and keep separate candidacies

@joint_social
title: Sign a social floor on health, housing and labour rights
subtitle: Cost: 2 resources. Better voter transfer; liberal and old-guard resistance.
choose-if: resources >= 2
unavailable-subtitle: The common campaign cannot be financed.
on-arrival: resources -= 2; pres_ko_joint_candidate = 1; pres_ko_joint_conversion = 0.86; pres_first_calc_mode = "opening_poll"; ko_relation += 5; labor_credibility += 3; public_trust += 2; barons_dissent += 5; ko_coalition_dissent += 3; news_headline = "KO withdraws for a democratic-social common ticket"
go-to: opening_poll

@joint_institutional
title: Make it a constitutional ticket with a modest social annex
subtitle: Cost: 1 resource. Easier for KO; Razem sees a liberal rescue operation.
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Even the joint legal operation needs staff and ballot infrastructure.
on-arrival: resources -= 1; pres_ko_joint_candidate = 1; pres_ko_joint_conversion = 0.82; pres_first_calc_mode = "opening_poll"; ko_relation += 8; constitutional_restraint += 4; public_trust += 2; razem_dissent += 8; labor_credibility -= 2; news_headline = "KO withdraws for a common constitutional candidate"
go-to: opening_poll

@calculate_first
on-arrival: {!
const clampPres = function(value, low, high) {
    return Math.max(low, Math.min(high, Number(value) || 0));
};
const ids = [
    "duda", "trzaskowski", "holownia", "bosak",
    "kosiniak", "left", "other"
];
const leftIntent = Number.isFinite(Number(Q.left_vote_intent))
    ? Number(Q.left_vote_intent) : 12.6;
// Preserve the 2015/2020 presidential squeeze until Lewica becomes a visibly
// larger electorate; above 16%, party support starts converting rapidly.
const leftBreakthrough = Math.max(0, leftIntent - 16);
const leftCampaignReach = clampPres(
    0.45 + (leftIntent - 12) * 0.11,
    0.35,
    1
);
const leftCampaignLift =
    ((Number(Q.party_unity) || 58) - 58) * 0.025 +
    ((Number(Q.public_trust) || 43) - 43) * 0.020 +
    ((Number(Q.media_capacity) || 16) - 16) * 0.018 +
    ((Number(Q.turnout_readiness) || 58) - 58) * 0.012 +
    ((Number(Q.primary_mandate) || 30) - 30) * 0.010 +
    (Number(Q.pres_bonus_left) || 0);
const leftSqueezed = leftIntent < 16 && !Q.pres_ko_joint_candidate;
const leftCeiling = leftSqueezed ? 6.5 : Infinity;
const raw = {
    duda:
        43.50 +
        ((Number(Q.pis_vote_intent) || 43.6) - 43.6) * 0.24 +
        (Number(Q.government_delivery) || 0) * 0.035 +
        (45 - (Number(Q.household_security) || 45)) * 0.012 +
        (Number(Q.pres_bonus_duda) || 0),
    trzaskowski:
        (Q.pres_2020_ko_kidawa ? 8.40 : 30.46) +
        ((Number(Q.ko_vote_intent) || 27.4) - 27.4) *
            (Q.pres_2020_ko_kidawa ? 0.12 : 0.24) +
        ((Number(Q.judicial_legitimacy) || 36) - 36) * 0.018 +
        (Number(Q.pres_bonus_trzaskowski) || 0),
    holownia:
        13.87 +
        ((Number(Q.public_trust) || 43) - 43) * -0.012 +
        (Number(Q.pres_bonus_holownia) || 0),
    bosak:
        6.78 +
        ((Number(Q.konf_vote_intent) || 6.8) - 6.8) * 0.32 +
        ((Number(Q.far_right_agenda) || 32) - 32) * 0.022 +
        (Number(Q.pres_bonus_bosak) || 0),
    kosiniak:
        2.36 +
        ((Number(Q.psl_vote_intent) || 8.6) - 8.6) * 0.11 +
        (Number(Q.pres_bonus_kosiniak) || 0),
    left:
        Math.min(
            leftCeiling,
            (Number(Q.presidential_candidate_base) || 2.2) +
                (leftIntent - 12.6) * 0.10 +
                leftBreakthrough * 1.30 +
                leftCampaignLift * leftCampaignReach
        ),
    other:
        0.81 + (Number(Q.pres_bonus_other) || 0)
};

if (Q.postal_election_stance == "Democratic legal front") {
    raw.trzaskowski += 0.25;
    raw.left += 0.10;
    raw.duda -= 0.15;
    Q.pres_postal_stance_effect =
        "The legal front modestly mobilises both democratic campaigns";
} else if (Q.postal_election_stance == "Gowin postponement bargain") {
    raw.duda += 0.12;
    raw.holownia += 0.10;
    raw.left -= 0.08;
    Q.pres_postal_stance_effect =
        "The postponement bargain rewards moderation outside the Left";
} else if (Q.postal_election_stance == "Boycott") {
    raw.left -= 0.45;
    raw.holownia += 0.12;
    Q.pres_postal_stance_effect =
        "The abandoned boycott line depresses Left conversion in the restored vote";
} else if (Q.postal_election_stance == "Compete and litigate") {
    raw.left += 0.25;
    Q.pres_postal_stance_effect =
        "Ballot preparation survives the legal challenge and aids the Left campaign";
} else if (Q.postal_election_stance == "General opposition protest") {
    raw.trzaskowski += 0.40;
    raw.left += 0.35;
    raw.duda -= 0.40;
    Q.pres_postal_stance_effect =
        "The protest that restored the ballot mobilises the democratic campaigns";
}

if (Q.pres_2020_ko_kidawa) {
    // The support KO's nominee cannot hold does not disappear into the
    // average: an anti-PiS electorate with no viable candidate of its own
    // moves to the campaigns that can still plausibly reach the runoff.
    const shed = 30.46 - 8.40;
    raw.holownia += shed * 0.50;
    raw.left += shed * 0.14;
    raw.kosiniak += shed * 0.13;
    raw.bosak += shed * 0.08;
    raw.duda += shed * 0.07;
    raw.other += shed * 0.08;
}

if (Q.pres_breakout_key && Q.pres_breakout_key != "none" &&
    raw[Q.pres_breakout_key] !== undefined) {
    raw[Q.pres_breakout_key] += Number(Q.pres_breakout_size) || 0;
}

if (Q.pres_ko_joint_candidate) {
    const displaced = Math.max(0, raw.trzaskowski);
    const conversion = clampPres(
        (Number(Q.pres_ko_joint_conversion) || 0.82) +
            ((Number(Q.ko_relation) || 60) - 60) * 0.0015 +
            ((Number(Q.party_unity) || 60) - 60) * 0.001,
        0.80,
        0.90
    );
    raw.trzaskowski = 0;
    raw.left += displaced * conversion;
    raw.holownia += displaced * 0.075;
    raw.duda += displaced * 0.025;
    raw.other += displaced * Math.max(0, 0.90 - conversion);
}

let noisePrefix = "pres_open_noise_";
if (Q.pres_first_calc_mode == "tracking_poll") {
    noisePrefix = "pres_track_noise_";
}
if (Q.pres_first_calc_mode == "first_result") {
    noisePrefix = "pres_r1_shock_";
}
for (const id of ids) {
    if (id == "trzaskowski" && Q.pres_ko_joint_candidate) {
        raw[id] = 0;
    } else {
        raw[id] = Math.max(
            id == "other" ? 0.05 : 0.15,
            raw[id] + (Number(Q[noisePrefix + id]) || 0)
        );
        if (id == "left" && leftSqueezed) {
            raw[id] = Math.min(leftCeiling, raw[id]);
        }
    }
}
const total = ids.reduce(function(sum, id) {
    return sum + raw[id];
}, 0);
const share = {};
for (const id of ids) {
    share[id] = raw[id] * 100 / Math.max(1, total);
}

const roundedShares = function(values) {
    const rounded = {};
    for (const id of ids) {
        rounded[id] = Math.round(values[id] * 10) / 10;
    }
    const roundedTotal = ids.reduce(function(sum, id) {
        return sum + rounded[id];
    }, 0);
    const residual = Math.round((100 - roundedTotal) * 10) / 10;
    let residualId = "other";
    if (rounded.other + residual < 0) {
        residualId = ids.slice().sort(function(left, right) {
            return rounded[right] - rounded[left];
        })[0];
    }
    rounded[residualId] =
        Math.round((rounded[residualId] + residual) * 10) / 10;
    return rounded;
};
const display = roundedShares(share);

if (Q.pres_first_calc_mode == "opening_poll" ||
    Q.pres_first_calc_mode == "tracking_poll") {
    for (const id of ids) {
        Q["pres_poll_" + id] = display[id];
    }
    if (Q.pres_first_calc_mode == "tracking_poll" &&
        Q.pres_debate_resolved) {
        Q.pres_debate_poll_shift =
            Math.round(
                (
                    Q.pres_poll_left -
                    (Number(Q.pres_debate_poll_before_left) || 0)
                ) * 10
            ) / 10;
    }
}

if (Q.pres_first_calc_mode == "first_result") {
    const wasNewCount = !Q.pres_first_round_complete;
    for (const id of ids) {
        Q["pres_r1_raw_" + id] = share[id];
        Q["pres_r1_display_" + id] = display[id];
    }
    const ordered = ids.filter(function(id) {
        return share[id] > 0.000001;
    }).sort(function(left, right) {
        if (Math.abs(share[right] - share[left]) > 0.0000001) {
            return share[right] - share[left];
        }
        return ids.indexOf(left) - ids.indexOf(right);
    });
    const names = {
        duda: "Andrzej Duda",
        trzaskowski: Q.pres_2020_ko_name || "Rafał Trzaskowski",
        holownia: "Szymon Hołownia",
        bosak: "Krzysztof Bosak",
        kosiniak: "Władysław Kosiniak-Kamysz",
        left: Q.presidential_candidate,
        other: "Other candidates"
    };
    Q.pres_r1_leader_key = ordered[0];
    Q.pres_r1_leader_name = names[ordered[0]];
    Q.pres_r1_runner_key = ordered[1] || ordered[0];
    Q.pres_r1_runner_name = names[Q.pres_r1_runner_key];
    Q.pres_finalist_a_key = Q.pres_r1_leader_key;
    Q.pres_finalist_a_name = Q.pres_r1_leader_name;
    Q.pres_finalist_b_key = Q.pres_r1_runner_key;
    Q.pres_finalist_b_name = Q.pres_r1_runner_name;
    Q.pres_first_round_majority =
        share[Q.pres_r1_leader_key] > 50 ? 1 : 0;

    const turnout = clampPres(
        64.51 +
            ((Number(Q.turnout_readiness) || 58) - 58) * 0.035 +
            (Number(Q.pres_turnout_bonus) || 0) * 0.18 +
            (Number(Q.pres_r1_turnout_shock) || 0),
        58,
        72
    );
    Q.pres_r1_turnout = Math.round(turnout * 100) / 100;
    Q.pres_r1_valid_votes = Math.round(
        19425459 * turnout / 64.51
    );
    const votes = {};
    let allocated = 0;
    for (const id of ids) {
        votes[id] = Math.floor(
            Q.pres_r1_valid_votes * share[id] / 100
        );
        allocated += votes[id];
    }
    votes[Q.pres_r1_leader_key] +=
        Q.pres_r1_valid_votes - allocated;
    const formatVotes = function(value) {
        return String(Math.round(value)).replace(
            /\B(?=(\d{3})+(?!\d))/g,
            " "
        );
    };
    for (const id of ids) {
        Q["pres_r1_votes_" + id] = votes[id];
        Q["pres_r1_votes_" + id + "_display"] =
            formatVotes(votes[id]);
    }
    Q.pres_r1_valid_votes_display =
        formatVotes(Q.pres_r1_valid_votes);
    Q.presidential_result =
        Math.round(share.left * 100) / 100;
    Q.pres_historical_benchmark = 2.22;
    Q.pres_expected_result = Math.round(
        (
            Number.isFinite(Number(Q.pres_poll_left))
                ? Number(Q.pres_poll_left)
                : Number(Q.presidential_candidate_base) || 2.2
        ) * 100
    ) / 100;
    Q.pres_expectation_gap = Math.round(
        (Q.presidential_result - Q.pres_expected_result) * 100
    ) / 100;
    Q.pres_historical_gap = Math.round(
        (Q.presidential_result - Q.pres_historical_benchmark) * 100
    ) / 100;
    const leftTransformed =
        ordered[0] == "left" || ordered[1] == "left";
    if (leftTransformed) {
        Q.pres_performance_band = "Party-system transformation";
        Q.pres_performance_level = 4;
    } else if (Q.presidential_result < 2.5) {
        Q.pres_performance_band = "Shattering disaster";
        Q.pres_performance_level = -3;
    } else if (Q.presidential_result < 4) {
        Q.pres_performance_band = "Severe defeat";
        Q.pres_performance_level = -2;
    } else if (Q.presidential_result < 5.5) {
        Q.pres_performance_band = "Disappointing or ambiguous";
        Q.pres_performance_level = -1;
    } else if (Q.presidential_result < 7.5) {
        Q.pres_performance_band = "Base held; broadly satisfying";
        Q.pres_performance_level = 1;
    } else if (Q.presidential_result < 10) {
        Q.pres_performance_band = "Strong result";
        Q.pres_performance_level = 2;
    } else {
        Q.pres_performance_band = "Breakthrough";
        Q.pres_performance_level = 3;
    }
    Q.pres_first_round_complete = 1;
    Q.pres_2020_phase = Q.pres_first_round_majority
        ? "Decided in the first round"
        : "Between rounds";

    if (Q.pres_first_round_majority) {
        // The KO row keeps its internal key through the count, but only an
        // actual Trzaskowski presidency may enter the Trzaskowski chapter.
        const electedKey =
            Q.pres_r1_leader_key == "trzaskowski" && Q.pres_2020_ko_kidawa
                ? "kidawa"
                : Q.pres_r1_leader_key;
        Q.pres_runoff_winner_key = electedKey;
        Q.pres_runoff_winner_name = Q.pres_r1_leader_name;
        Q.pres_2020_president_elect_key = electedKey;
        Q.pres_2020_president_elect_name = Q.pres_r1_leader_name;
        Q.pres_runoff_complete = 1;
        Q.trzaskowski_won = electedKey == "trzaskowski" ? 1 : 0;
        Q.left_president = 0;
        if (Q.trzaskowski_won) {
            Q.trz_inauguration_status =
                "President-elect — certification pending";
            Q.pres_2020_phase = "Certification pending";
        }
    }
    const presWinnerImages2020 = {
        "Andrzej Duda": "img/poland/events/pres-candidate-duda-2020.webp",
        "Rafał Trzaskowski": "img/poland/events/pres-candidate-trzaskowski.webp",
        "Małgorzata Kidawa-Błońska": "img/poland/events/pres-candidate-kidawa-2020.webp",
        "Szymon Hołownia": "img/poland/events/pres-candidate-holownia-2020.webp",
        "Krzysztof Bosak": "img/poland/events/pres-candidate-bosak.webp",
        "Władysław Kosiniak-Kamysz": "img/poland/events/pres-candidate-kosiniak-2020.webp",
        "Robert Biedroń": "img/poland/events/pres-candidate-biedron-2020.webp",
        "Adrian Zandberg": "img/poland/events/adrian-zandberg-2020.webp",
        "Agnieszka Dziemianowicz-Bąk": "img/poland/cards/advisor-dziemianowicz-bak.webp",
        "Anna-Maria Żukowska": "img/poland/cards/advisor-zukowska.webp",
        "Katarzyna Kotula": "img/poland/cards/advisor-kotula.webp",
        "Magdalena Biejat": "img/poland/cards/advisor-biejat.webp"
    };
    this.game.scenes[
        "poland_presidential_election.first_count"
    ].faceImage = Q.pres_first_round_majority
        ? presWinnerImages2020[Q.pres_runoff_winner_name] ||
            "img/poland/events/presidential-ballot-2020.webp"
        : "img/poland/events/presidential-ballot-2020.webp";
    if (wasNewCount) {
        const level = Number(Q.pres_performance_level) || 0;
        const previousFailure = Q.pres_feedback_active &&
            (Number(Q.pres_feedback_direction) || 0) < 0 && level < 0;
        let duration = level == -3 || level >= 3 ? 12 :
            (level == -2 || level == 2 ? 10 :
            (level == -1 ? 7 : 8));
        let consideration = level == -3 ? -6 :
            (level == -2 ? -3.8 :
            (level == -1 ? -1.4 :
            (level == 1 ? 1.2 :
            (level == 2 ? 2.7 :
            (level == 3 ? 4.2 : 5.5)))));
        let feedbackTurnout = level == -3 ? -5 :
            (level == -2 ? -3.1 :
            (level == -1 ? -1.0 :
            (level == 1 ? 1.4 :
            (level == 2 ? 2.4 :
            (level == 3 ? 3.4 : 4.5)))));
        if (previousFailure) {
            duration = Math.min(12, duration + 2);
            consideration *= 1.15;
            feedbackTurnout *= 1.15;
            Q.pres_feedback_reinforcements =
                (Number(Q.pres_feedback_reinforcements) || 0) + 1;
        }
        const expectationAdjustment = Math.max(
            -1.5,
            Math.min(1.5, (Number(Q.pres_expectation_gap) || 0) * 0.25)
        );
        consideration += expectationAdjustment;
        feedbackTurnout += expectationAdjustment * 0.65;
        if (level == 1) {
            consideration = Math.max(0.5, consideration);
            feedbackTurnout = Math.max(0.6, feedbackTurnout);
        }
        Q.pres_feedback_active = 1;
        Q.pres_feedback_source = "2020 presidential first round";
        Q.pres_feedback_direction = level < 0 ? -1 : 1;
        Q.pres_feedback_duration = duration;
        Q.pres_feedback_months_remaining = duration;
        Q.pres_feedback_decay_factor = 1;
        Q.pres_feedback_consideration =
            Math.round(consideration * 100) / 100;
        Q.pres_feedback_turnout =
            Math.round(feedbackTurnout * 100) / 100;
        Q.pres_feedback_consideration_current =
            Q.pres_feedback_consideration;
        Q.pres_feedback_turnout_current = Q.pres_feedback_turnout;
        Q.pres_feedback_leadership_pressure = 0;
        Q.pres_feedback_leadership_challenge = 0;
        Q.pres_feedback_donor_loss = 0;
        Q.pres_feedback_activist_loss = 0;
        Q.pres_feedback_media_loss = 0;
        Q.pres_feedback_faction_pressure = 0;
        Q.pres_feedback_tactical_flight = 0;
        Q.pres_feedback_base_certainty = 0;
        Q.pres_feedback_squeeze_protection = 0;
        if (level == -3) {
            Q.pres_feedback_leadership_pressure = 85;
            Q.pres_feedback_leadership_challenge = 1;
            Q.pres_feedback_donor_loss = 2;
            Q.pres_feedback_activist_loss = 6;
            Q.pres_feedback_media_loss = 4;
            Q.pres_feedback_faction_pressure = 8;
            Q.pres_feedback_tactical_flight = 6;
            Q.resources -= 2;
            Q.organiser_energy -= 6;
            Q.media_capacity -= 4;
            Q.media_access -= 5;
            Q.leadership_authority -= 9;
            Q.list_confidence -= 8;
            Q.winner_reputation -= 7;
            Q.electoral_viability -= 5;
            Q.party_unity -= 7;
            Q.barons_dissent += 7;
            Q.spring_dissent += 8;
            Q.labor_dissent += 5;
            Q.progressives_dissent += 7;
            Q.razem_dissent += 6;
        } else if (level == -2) {
            Q.pres_feedback_leadership_pressure = 65;
            Q.pres_feedback_leadership_challenge = 1;
            Q.pres_feedback_donor_loss = 1;
            Q.pres_feedback_activist_loss = 4;
            Q.pres_feedback_media_loss = 3;
            Q.pres_feedback_faction_pressure = 6;
            Q.pres_feedback_tactical_flight = 4;
            Q.resources -= 1;
            Q.organiser_energy -= 4;
            Q.media_capacity -= 3;
            Q.media_access -= 3;
            Q.leadership_authority -= 6;
            Q.list_confidence -= 5;
            Q.winner_reputation -= 4;
            Q.electoral_viability -= 3;
            Q.party_unity -= 5;
            Q.barons_dissent += 5;
            Q.spring_dissent += 6;
            Q.labor_dissent += 3;
            Q.progressives_dissent += 5;
            Q.razem_dissent += 4;
        } else if (level == -1) {
            Q.pres_feedback_leadership_pressure = 30;
            Q.pres_feedback_activist_loss = 1;
            Q.pres_feedback_media_loss = 1;
            Q.pres_feedback_faction_pressure = 2;
            Q.pres_feedback_tactical_flight = 1;
            Q.organiser_energy -= 1;
            Q.media_capacity -= 1;
            Q.media_access -= 1;
            Q.leadership_authority -= 2;
            Q.list_confidence -= 2;
            Q.winner_reputation -= 1;
            Q.party_unity -= 2;
            Q.spring_dissent += 2;
            Q.progressives_dissent += 2;
            Q.razem_dissent += 1;
        } else {
            Q.pres_feedback_base_certainty = level == 1 ? 65 :
                (level == 2 ? 78 : 92);
            Q.pres_feedback_squeeze_protection = 1;
            Q.party_unity += level == 1 ? 3 : (level == 2 ? 4 : 6);
            Q.organiser_energy += level == 1 ? 2 : (level == 2 ? 3 : 5);
            Q.media_capacity += level == 1 ? 1 : (level == 2 ? 2 : 4);
            Q.media_access += level == 1 ? 1 : (level == 2 ? 2 : 4);
            Q.leadership_authority += level == 1 ? 3 :
                (level == 2 ? 4 : 6);
            Q.list_confidence += level == 1 ? 5 :
                (level == 2 ? 6 : 8);
            Q.winner_reputation += level == 1 ? 2 :
                (level == 2 ? 4 : 6);
            Q.electoral_viability += level == 1 ? 2 :
                (level == 2 ? 3 : 5);
            Q.tactical_desertion_to_ko = Math.max(
                0,
                Q.tactical_desertion_to_ko - (level == 1 ? 2 : 4)
            );
            Q.tactical_desertion_to_abstention = Math.max(
                0,
                Q.tactical_desertion_to_abstention - (level == 1 ? 1 : 3)
            );
            Q.barons_dissent -= level == 1 ? 1 : 2;
            Q.spring_dissent -= level == 1 ? 1 : 2;
            Q.progressives_dissent -= level == 1 ? 1 : 2;
        }
        Q.pres_feedback_tactical_current =
            Q.pres_feedback_tactical_flight;
        const holowniaResult = Math.max(
            0,
            Number(Q.pres_r1_display_holownia) ||
                Number(Q.pres_poll_holownia) || 0
        );
        const p2050Conversion = Math.max(
            0.25,
            Math.min(5, (holowniaResult - 2) * 0.32)
        );
        Q.p2050_emerged = 1;
        Q.p2050_relation = Math.max(
            Number(Q.p2050_relation) || 0,
            Math.round(18 + Math.min(18, holowniaResult * 0.75))
        );
        Q.p2050_leader = "Szymon Hołownia";
        Q.p2050_poll_momentum =
            (Number(Q.p2050_poll_momentum) || 0) + p2050Conversion;
        Q.ko_poll_momentum =
            (Number(Q.ko_poll_momentum) || 0) - p2050Conversion * 0.55;
        Q.psl_poll_momentum =
            (Number(Q.psl_poll_momentum) || 0) - p2050Conversion * 0.15;
        Q.other_poll_momentum =
            (Number(Q.other_poll_momentum) || 0) - p2050Conversion * 0.20;

        // KO's candidate missing the runoff is not a bad night. The whole
        // Civic claim on the opposition is that only KO can reach the second
        // round and therefore everybody else must stand aside; a first round
        // that says otherwise ends the claim, and no later poll recovery
        // gives it back. One scalar carries the size of the failure into
        // every later model rather than each one re-reading the count.
        const koShareR1 = Math.round(share.trzaskowski * 100) / 100;
        if (!Q.pres_ko_joint_candidate && ordered[0] != "trzaskowski" &&
            ordered[1] != "trzaskowski") {
            Q.ko_2020_runoff_miss = 1;
            Q.ko_2020_r1_share = koShareR1;
            Q.ko_2020_r1_rank = ordered.indexOf("trzaskowski") + 1;
            Q.ko_2020_r1_rank_label = Q.ko_2020_r1_rank == 3
                ? "third"
                : (Q.ko_2020_r1_rank == 4 ? "fourth" : "outside the first four");
            Q.ko_2020_finalists =
                Q.pres_r1_leader_name + " and " + Q.pres_r1_runner_name;
            Q.ko_2020_miss_band = koShareR1 >= 14
                ? "Beaten into third"
                : (koShareR1 >= 8 ? "Humiliation" : "Annihilation");
            Q.ko_2020_humiliation = Math.round(
                Math.max(14, Math.min(60, (20 - koShareR1) * 4))
            );
            const koFall = Q.ko_2020_humiliation;
            Q.ko_hegemony_broken = 1;
            Q.ko_poll_momentum =
                (Number(Q.ko_poll_momentum) || 0) - (1.8 + koFall * 0.06);
            Q.ko_poll = Math.max(
                6, (Number(Q.ko_poll) || 27.4) - koFall * 0.09
            );
            Q.ko_coalition_dissent = (Number(Q.ko_coalition_dissent) || 0) +
                Math.round(9 + koFall * 0.35);
            Q.ko_cohesion = Math.max(12, Math.round(
                (Number(Q.ko_cohesion) || 62) - (7 + koFall * 0.30)
            ));
            Q.ko_collapse_shock = (Number(Q.ko_collapse_shock) || 0) +
                Math.round(koFall * 0.55);
            Q.ko_ai_resources = Math.max(
                0, (Number(Q.ko_ai_resources) || 7) - 2
            );
            Q.ko_relation = Math.max(0, (Number(Q.ko_relation) || 0) - 4);
            // The wing that chose the candidate loses the argument about who
            // KO is for: a flopped primary winner vindicates the mayors, a
            // flopped mayor vindicates the people who never wanted him.
            Q.ko_social_liberal_share = Math.max(0, Math.min(100,
                (Number(Q.ko_social_liberal_share) || 42) +
                    (Q.pres_2020_ko_kidawa ? 9 : -9)
            ));
            Q.ko_classical_liberal_share = 100 - Q.ko_social_liberal_share;
            // Nobody votes tactically for a party that has just proved it
            // cannot reach a runoff. This is the hegemony, and it is the part
            // that does not come back.
            Q.tactical_desertion_to_ko = Math.max(
                0, (Number(Q.tactical_desertion_to_ko) || 0) * 0.35
            );
            Q.pres_feedback_tactical_flight = Math.round(
                (Number(Q.pres_feedback_tactical_flight) || 0) * 45
            ) / 100;
            Q.pres_feedback_tactical_current = Q.pres_feedback_tactical_flight;
            Q.opposition_list_pressure = Math.max(
                0,
                (Number(Q.opposition_list_pressure) || 0) - (4 + koFall * 0.12)
            );
            Q.party_system_left_pull = (Number(Q.party_system_left_pull) || 0) +
                Math.round(2 + koFall * 0.10);
            Q.left_poll_momentum =
                (Number(Q.left_poll_momentum) || 0) + koFall * 0.012;
            Q.konf_poll_momentum =
                (Number(Q.konf_poll_momentum) || 0) + koFall * 0.008;
            Q.historical_pressure_last = "KO's " + koShareR1 +
                "% leaves the Civic bloc out of the runoff between " +
                Q.ko_2020_finalists;
        }
    }
    const presidentialMapModel = (typeof window !== "undefined"
        ? window : globalThis).polandElectionModel;
    presidentialMapModel.archivePresident(Q,
        presidentialMapModel.allocatePresident({
            state: Q,
            key: "2020-06-r1",
            label: "2020 presidential election — first round",
            round: 1,
            candidates: ids.map(function(id) {
                return {
                    id: id,
                    name: names[id],
                    family: {
                        duda: "pis", trzaskowski: "ko", holownia: "p2050",
                        bosak: "konf", kosiniak: "psl", left: "left",
                        other: "other"
                    }[id],
                    share: share[id]
                };
            })
        })
    );
    Q.news_headline = Q.pres_first_round_majority
        ? Q.pres_r1_leader_name +
            " wins the presidency in the first round"
        : Q.pres_r1_leader_name + " and " +
            Q.pres_r1_runner_name + " enter the runoff";
}
!}

@opening_poll
title: The opening tracking poll
new-page: true
call: poland_presidential_election.calculate_first

= A race with error bars

The poll has a **±1.8 point working margin**. It is sampled from the same party,
trust, organisation and turnout state used by the wider electorate model.

Postal-election carryover: **[+ pres_postal_stance_effect +]**.

<div class="poll-table">
<div class="poll-row"><span class="party party-pis"><b>Duda</b></span><span>[+ pres_poll_duda +]%</span><span>PiS</span></div>
[? if pres_ko_joint_candidate = 0: <div class="poll-row"><span class="party party-ko"><b>[+ pres_2020_ko_surname +]</b></span><span>[+ pres_poll_trzaskowski +]%</span><span>KO</span></div>?]
<div class="poll-row"><span class="party party-p2050"><b>Hołownia</b></span><span>[+ pres_poll_holownia +]%</span><span>civic campaign</span></div>
<div class="poll-row"><span class="party party-konf"><b>Bosak</b></span><span>[+ pres_poll_bosak +]%</span><span>Konf.</span></div>
<div class="poll-row"><span class="party party-psl"><b>Kosiniak-Kamysz</b></span><span>[+ pres_poll_kosiniak +]%</span><span>PSL</span></div>
<div class="poll-row"><span class="party party-lewica"><b>[+ presidential_candidate +]</b></span><span>[+ pres_poll_left +]%</span><span>[? if pres_ko_joint_candidate: common ticket?][? if pres_ko_joint_candidate = 0: Left?]</span></div>
<div class="poll-row"><span><b>Other</b></span><span>[+ pres_poll_other +]%</span><span>combined</span></div>
</div>

- @campaign_menu: Open the two-move campaign board

@campaign_menu
title: Two moves before the first ballot
new-page: true

= Campaign board — [+ pres_first_actions_remaining +] moves remain

Each operation can be used once. Polling measures the field; it does not reveal
the saved election-day shock.

- @campaign_digital
- @campaign_work
- @campaign_equality
- @campaign_counties
- @campaign_constitution
- @campaign_insurgent

@campaign_digital
title: Buy reach: video, targeting and rapid response
subtitle: Cost: 2 resources. Strongest where a media operation already exists.
view-if: pres_campaign_digital = 0
choose-if: resources >= 2
unavailable-subtitle: The campaign lacks cash and production capacity.
on-arrival: resources -= 2; pres_campaign_digital = 1; pres_first_actions_remaining -= 1; pres_bonus_left += 0.95 + media_capacity * 0.004; media_capacity += 3; pres_turnout_bonus += 0.4; news_headline = "The Left buys a professional digital finish"

An agency, a studio week and a rapid-response desk that answers within the hour
rather than the following morning. In a pandemic campaign where nobody can fill
a hall, the feed is the hall, and for the first time this campaign is buying
its own reach rather than waiting for a booking.

It is the single most expensive thing on the board, and the money is gone
whatever happens on the ballot. What it produces is a candidate people have
seen — which, at two per cent, is most of the problem.

- @campaign_next
- @campaign_done

@campaign_work
title: Put work, rent and public health on every podium
subtitle: Free. Distinctive first-round ownership; KO dislikes the contrast.
view-if: pres_campaign_work = 0
on-arrival: pres_campaign_work = 1; pres_first_actions_remaining -= 1; pres_bonus_left += 0.85; labor_credibility += 4; workers_support += 2; public_sector_support += 2; razem_dissent -= 3; ko_relation -= 2; news_headline = "The presidential campaign becomes a social argument"

Every appearance runs on the same three subjects: what people are being paid
during the epidemic, what they are paying in rent, and what the health service
has left after five years of announcements. The nurses' union sends speakers
without being asked.

KO's staff complain that this is a campaign against the opposition rather than
against Duda, and complain about it publicly, which does the argument no harm
at all.

- @campaign_next
- @campaign_done

@campaign_equality
title: Give women and equality movements the closing week
subtitle: Cost: 1 resource. Mobilisation with a conservative-caucus price.
view-if: pres_campaign_equality = 0
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: The campaign cannot support the organising network.
on-arrival: resources -= 1; pres_campaign_equality = 1; pres_first_actions_remaining -= 1; pres_bonus_left += 0.82; feminist_trust += 5; women_support += 3; young_support += 2; pres_turnout_bonus += 0.6; barons_dissent += 5; news_headline = "Equality movements enter the presidential ground campaign"

The organisations that filled the streets in the autumn are given the closing
week rather than a photograph: their speakers, their lists, their choice of
where the candidate stands. It is the most energetic ten days the campaign
has, and the youngest crowd it will ever draw.

The old guard in three voivodeships stop returning calls. They are not
threatening anything specific; they are simply making it known that this was
not the campaign they were promised.

- @campaign_next
- @campaign_done

@campaign_counties
title: Trade studio time for a county-by-county tour
subtitle: Cost: 1 resource. Local reach and a small opening among PSL voters.
view-if: pres_campaign_counties = 0
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Too few buses, organisers and county offices are available.
on-arrival: resources -= 1; pres_campaign_counties = 1; pres_first_actions_remaining -= 1; pres_bonus_left += 0.72; pres_bonus_kosiniak -= 0.10; local_network += 4; rural_support += 2; pres_turnout_bonus += 0.35; psl_relation += 2; news_headline = "The candidate leaves Warsaw for the county map"

The bus does thirty towns in eleven days, most of them places where the party's
entire local presence is one retired teacher with a mailing list. The meetings
are small and the local press comes to all of them, because nobody else has
bothered to visit.

Kosiniak-Kamysz's people notice, and are less friendly about it than their
public statements suggest. The national bulletins do not notice at all.

- @campaign_next
- @campaign_done

@campaign_constitution
title: Build the democratic-constitutional front early
subtitle: Free. Weaker first-round distinction; stronger runoff bridges.
view-if: pres_campaign_constitution = 0
on-arrival: pres_campaign_constitution = 1; pres_first_actions_remaining -= 1; pres_bonus_left += 0.48; pres_bonus_trzaskowski += 0.12 if pres_ko_joint_candidate = 0; pres_runoff_preparation += 0.55; ko_relation += 5; constitutional_restraint += 3; public_trust += 2; razem_dissent += 4; news_headline = "The campaign rehearses a democratic runoff coalition"

The campaign starts behaving in June like a campaign that expects to matter in
July: shared platforms on the courts, a common line on the postal-vote
scandal, and a deliberate refusal to attack anyone who might have to be
negotiated with in a fortnight.

It buys standing in the room where the runoff will be decided. It also spends
the first round, and Razem's members say so — at length, in writing, and to
journalists.

- @campaign_next
- @campaign_done

@campaign_insurgent
title: Turn the nominee loose on an improvised insurgent tour
subtitle: Free fallback. Candidate visibility without a durable machine.
view-if: pres_campaign_insurgent = 0
on-arrival: {!
Q.pres_campaign_insurgent = 1;
Q.pres_first_actions_remaining -= 1;
Q.pres_bonus_left +=
    0.52 + (Number(Q.presidential_candidate_base) || 0) * 0.05;
Q.media_capacity += 1;
Q.organiser_energy -= 2;
Q.public_trust += 1;
Q.news_headline =
    Q.presidential_candidate + " runs outside the headquarters script";
!}

The schedule is abandoned and the candidate simply goes: markets, hospital car
parks, a picket, three local radio stations in one afternoon, a livestream from
the back of a car. It costs nothing because there is nothing to pay for.

Some of it is better than anything the office would have produced. None of it
is repeatable, and the staff who spent the spring building a structure watch a
fortnight of improvisation go past without leaving a list, a rota or a single
new branch behind it.

- @campaign_next
- @campaign_done

@campaign_next
title: Return to the campaign board
view-if: pres_first_actions_remaining > 0
go-to: campaign_menu

@campaign_done
title: The last national debate is tomorrow
view-if: pres_first_actions_remaining <= 0
go-to: debate

@debate
# prose-audit: Grade A — The between-question framings and the per-nominee answer sets were always a real piece of authorship; each answer now also reports what the studio, the parishes and our own organisers did with it, and the spin room writes the night before it reprints the recap.
title: The last national debate
face-image: img/poland/events/tvp-headquarters.webp
new-page: true
on-arrival: pres_first_calc_mode = "tracking_poll"
call: poland_presidential_election.calculate_first

= 17 June 2020 — TVP, Warsaw

All eleven candidates receive the same five one-minute questions and one free
closing minute. TVP permits no formal rebuttals, but it cannot stop a candidate
from using their own clock to answer another lectern.

Rather than repeat six timers, the campaign treats the broadcast as three
linked decisions. Each choice sets how **[+ presidential_candidate +]** joins
two answers into one argument—and whether to spend precious seconds replying
directly to a rival.

[? if presidential_candidate = "Adrian Zandberg": Zandberg has already shown
that a crowded television debate can change how a national audience sees him.
The campaign expects more than survival.?]

- @debate_begin: Take the Left's lectern

@debate_begin
title: Take the Left's lectern
on-arrival: {!
if (!Q.pres_debate_initialized) {
    Q.pres_debate_initialized = 1;
    Q.pres_debate_poll_before_left =
        Number(Q.pres_poll_left) || 0;
    Q.pres_debate_stops_remaining = 3;
    Q.news_headline =
        "The full presidential field enters TVP's final debate";

    const voices = {
        "Robert Biedroń": {
            frame: [
                "Defend asylum law and a secular school without apology",
                "Answer Duda: neither refugees nor pupils need PiS permission",
                "Lead with controlled asylum and freedom of conscience"
            ],
            rights: [
                "Make equal families and evidence-led vaccination one promise",
                "Answer Bosak: my family is not your campaign prop",
                "Promise partnerships now and build trust before vaccine rules"
            ],
            close: [
                "Close on an open Poland where every family belongs",
                "Answer Duda with the citizens his presidency left outside",
                "Challenge Hołownia: change needs more than a new face"
            ]
        },
        "Adrian Zandberg": {
            frame: [
                "Put a capable secular state above bishops and border panic",
                "Answer Duda: strength is law and capacity, not scapegoats",
                "Reject forced quotas and move religion outside public school"
            ],
            rights: [
                "Join equal dignity to a universal public-health service",
                "Answer Bosak: rights do not close wards; underfunding does",
                "Secure civil rights while keeping the vaccine mandate cautious"
            ],
            close: [
                "Close on wages, rents and a social republic",
                "Answer Duda with five years of signatures against working people",
                "Challenge Hołownia: the duopoly is economic, not only partisan"
            ]
        },
        "Agnieszka Dziemianowicz-Bąk": {
            frame: [
                "Defend the secular classroom as a common public institution",
                "Answer Duda: public schools cannot sort children by belief",
                "Protect secular access while leaving religion to families"
            ],
            rights: [
                "Pair equal family law with trusted, universal vaccination",
                "Answer Bosak: public safety needs trust, not scapegoats",
                "Set a rights floor and earn consent through public health"
            ],
            close: [
                "Close on schools, hospitals and dignified work",
                "Answer Duda with the public institutions weakened on his watch",
                "Challenge Hołownia to say who pays for political renewal"
            ]
        },
        "Anna-Maria Żukowska": {
            frame: [
                "Reject both loaded premises before the clock can trap you",
                "Answer Duda directly and name the diversion",
                "Give a clipped defence of controlled asylum and voluntary religion"
            ],
            rights: [
                "Say yes to equal families and science—without qualifications",
                "Turn Bosak's culture-war premise back on him",
                "Defend partnerships and voluntary vaccination in one sharp line"
            ],
            close: [
                "Close with the line every studio will have to replay",
                "Put Duda's record on trial, signature by signature",
                "Tell Hołownia that a new logo is not a new politics"
            ]
        },
        "Katarzyna Kotula": {
            frame: [
                "Speak for pupils and families excluded by the Church's rules",
                "Answer Duda with the people his politics pushes outside",
                "Make religion voluntary and equal treatment non-negotiable"
            ],
            rights: [
                "Demand full family equality and vaccination led by evidence",
                "Answer Bosak with the families he would deny",
                "Protect partnerships now and organise for the rest"
            ],
            close: [
                "Give women and equality movements the final minute",
                "Answer Duda with five years of blocked rights",
                "Challenge Hołownia to choose a side on equality"
            ]
        },
        "Magdalena Biejat": {
            frame: [
                "Ground solidarity in the everyday security of every family",
                "Answer Duda: security begins with homes, not exclusion",
                "Tie controlled reception and voluntary religion to local capacity"
            ],
            rights: [
                "Make family security mean equal law and accessible vaccination",
                "Answer Bosak with care work, rent and real family life",
                "Win partnerships and build vaccination through neighbourhood trust"
            ],
            close: [
                "Close on rent, care and the homes people can afford",
                "Answer Duda with the families his economic record squeezed",
                "Challenge Hołownia: renewal without social guarantees is branding"
            ]
        }
    };
    const voice = voices[Q.presidential_candidate] || voices["Robert Biedroń"];
    Q.pres_debate_frame_signature_title = voice.frame[0];
    Q.pres_debate_frame_reply_title = voice.frame[1];
    Q.pres_debate_frame_cautious_title = voice.frame[2];
    Q.pres_debate_rights_signature_title = voice.rights[0];
    Q.pres_debate_rights_reply_title = voice.rights[1];
    Q.pres_debate_rights_cautious_title = voice.rights[2];
    Q.pres_debate_close_signature_title = voice.close[0];
    Q.pres_debate_close_duda_title = voice.close[1];
    Q.pres_debate_close_holownia_title = voice.close[2];
}
!}
go-to: debate_frame

@debate_frame
title: Refugees and First Communion
subtitle: Foreign policy and the place of religion in public schools.
new-page: true
max-visits: 1
view-if: pres_debate_frame_done = 0

The moderator moves from compulsory refugee relocation to preparing children
for First Communion during religion lessons. These are separate one-minute
answers; the political test is whether they sound like the same candidate.

Duda has already cast both questions as matters of national control and
parental choice. There is no rebuttal bell, but **[+ presidential_candidate +]**
may use part of either answer to challenge his frame.

- @debate_frame_direct
- @debate_frame_material
- @debate_frame_reassure

@debate_frame_direct
title: [+ pres_debate_frame_signature_title +]
subtitle: Use [+ presidential_candidate +]'s strongest register; conservative caucuses will own the backlash.
on-arrival: {!
const scores = {
    "Robert Biedroń": 2.2,
    "Adrian Zandberg": 2.3,
    "Agnieszka Dziemianowicz-Bąk": 2.5,
    "Anna-Maria Żukowska": 2.2,
    "Katarzyna Kotula": 2.4,
    "Magdalena Biejat": 2.1
};
Q.pres_debate_frame_done = 1;
Q.pres_debate_stops_remaining -= 1;
Q.pres_debate_score += scores[Q.presidential_candidate] || 2;
Q.pres_debate_frame_line = Q.pres_debate_frame_signature_title;
Q.progressive_credibility += 2;
Q.minority_safety += 2;
Q.barons_dissent += 3;
Q.news_headline =
    Q.presidential_candidate + " gives the opening questions a distinct Left answer";
!}

The two answers are joined without the join being announced. Relocation and the
catechism are treated as one question about who is allowed to belong to a
public institution, and the minute is spent on that rather than on Duda's
framing of either.

The bishops' conference is unhappy by Thursday and says so. So are two of our
own regional chairs, in a message they intended to be private. The clip that
survives the night is the one where the candidate declines to apologise for
the answer.

- @debate_rights_health: The fourth and fifth questions

@debate_frame_material
title: [+ pres_debate_frame_reply_title +]
subtitle: Reply to Duda from the candidate's own clock; sharper contrast, less room for the full answer.
on-arrival: {!
const scores = {
    "Robert Biedroń": 2,
    "Adrian Zandberg": 2.4,
    "Agnieszka Dziemianowicz-Bąk": 2.4,
    "Anna-Maria Żukowska": 2.5,
    "Katarzyna Kotula": 2.2,
    "Magdalena Biejat": 2.1
};
Q.pres_debate_frame_done = 1;
Q.pres_debate_stops_remaining -= 1;
Q.pres_debate_score += scores[Q.presidential_candidate] || 2;
Q.pres_debate_frame_line = Q.pres_debate_frame_reply_title;
Q.president_relation -= 3;
Q.media_capacity += 1;
Q.news_headline =
    Q.presidential_candidate + " answers Duda from the Left's allotted minute";
!}

Thirty of the sixty seconds are spent on the President rather than on the
question, which is the trade: a sharper contrast bought with the half of the
answer where the Left's own position was supposed to go.

Duda has no right of reply and does not need one — the studio hands him the
next question anyway. But there is now a recording of the incumbent being
addressed directly by a candidate polling in the low single figures, and it
does not look the way his staff expected it to look.

- @debate_rights_health: The fourth and fifth questions

@debate_frame_reassure
title: [+ pres_debate_frame_cautious_title +]
subtitle: A candidate-specific compromise; reassures moderates and lowers the ceiling.
on-arrival: {!
const scores = {
    "Robert Biedroń": 1,
    "Adrian Zandberg": 1.2,
    "Agnieszka Dziemianowicz-Bąk": 1.5,
    "Anna-Maria Żukowska": 1.1,
    "Katarzyna Kotula": 0.9,
    "Magdalena Biejat": 1.4
};
Q.pres_debate_frame_done = 1;
Q.pres_debate_stops_remaining -= 1;
Q.pres_debate_score += scores[Q.presidential_candidate] || 1;
Q.pres_debate_frame_line = Q.pres_debate_frame_cautious_title;
Q.psl_relation += 2;
Q.barons_dissent -= 2;
Q.progressives_dissent += 3;
Q.news_headline =
    Q.presidential_candidate + " chooses reassurance in the opening answers";
!}

Both answers are built to be unobjectionable to a viewer who has not decided
anything: controlled, lawful, respectful of what families choose for their own
children. Nobody watching is offended. Nobody watching writes it down either.

The PSL people are pleasantly surprised and mention it. The equality
organisations that have been supplying volunteers spend the following morning
asking each other whether that was the position all along, and the campaign
does not have a good answer ready.

- @debate_rights_health: The fourth and fifth questions

@debate_rights_health
title: Same-sex families and a COVID vaccine
subtitle: A loaded culture-war premise followed by a hypothetical health question.
new-page: true
max-visits: 1
view-if: pres_debate_rights_done = 0

The fourth and fifth questions collapse partnerships, marriage and adoption
into one test, then ask whether a future vaccine should be compulsory. Bosak
uses his clocks to turn both into warnings about coercion. His premise is still
hanging in the studio when the microphone reaches the Left.

- @debate_rights_full
- @debate_rights_dignity
- @debate_rights_cautious

@debate_rights_full
title: [+ pres_debate_rights_signature_title +]
subtitle: Answer both questions in [+ presidential_candidate +]'s strongest register.
on-arrival: {!
const scores = {
    "Robert Biedroń": 2.6,
    "Adrian Zandberg": 2.3,
    "Agnieszka Dziemianowicz-Bąk": 2.4,
    "Anna-Maria Żukowska": 2.4,
    "Katarzyna Kotula": 2.7,
    "Magdalena Biejat": 2.3
};
Q.pres_debate_rights_done = 1;
Q.pres_debate_stops_remaining -= 1;
Q.pres_debate_score += scores[Q.presidential_candidate] || 2.2;
Q.pres_debate_rights_line = Q.pres_debate_rights_signature_title;
Q.feminist_trust += 3;
Q.progressive_credibility += 2;
Q.barons_dissent += 3;
Q.news_headline =
    Q.presidential_candidate + " joins equal citizenship to public health";
!}

Partnerships, marriage, adoption and a vaccine are answered as one subject:
what the state owes people it has decided not to think about. There is no
hedging clause anywhere in the minute, which after four hours of hedging is
itself the effect.

Bosak's premise is left standing in the studio, unaddressed and now visibly
somebody else's. The counter-mobilisation starts in the parishes the same
weekend, and so does a run of small donations from people who have never given
the party anything before.

- @debate_economy_close: The last question and the free minute

@debate_rights_dignity
title: [+ pres_debate_rights_reply_title +]
subtitle: Answer Bosak directly, then recover the policy argument before the clock expires.
on-arrival: {!
const scores = {
    "Robert Biedroń": 2.2,
    "Adrian Zandberg": 2.4,
    "Agnieszka Dziemianowicz-Bąk": 2.3,
    "Anna-Maria Żukowska": 2.5,
    "Katarzyna Kotula": 2.6,
    "Magdalena Biejat": 2.2
};
Q.pres_debate_rights_done = 1;
Q.pres_debate_stops_remaining -= 1;
Q.pres_debate_score += scores[Q.presidential_candidate] || 2.2;
Q.pres_debate_rights_line = Q.pres_debate_rights_reply_title;
Q.public_trust += 2;
Q.health_policy_pressure += 1;
Q.last_policy_stage = "Proposal";
Q.last_policy_authority = "Presidential candidate";
Q.last_policy_implementation = 0;
Q.media_capacity += 1;
Q.konf_relation -= 2;
Q.news_headline =
    Q.presidential_candidate + " answers Bosak without surrendering the question";
!}

The reply is direct and short enough to leave room for the policy: Bosak's
warning about coercion is answered on its own terms, and then the last twenty
seconds are used for what a partnership act and a vaccination programme
actually consist of.

It is the answer that reads best in transcript and worst in a clip, because
half of it is an argument with a man most viewers have not been following.
Konfederacja's channels decide he won it; nobody else does.

- @debate_economy_close: The last question and the free minute

@debate_rights_cautious
title: [+ pres_debate_rights_cautious_title +]
subtitle: A narrower commitment in the nominee's own voice, with a lower ceiling.
on-arrival: {!
const scores = {
    "Robert Biedroń": 0.8,
    "Adrian Zandberg": 1.2,
    "Agnieszka Dziemianowicz-Bąk": 1.5,
    "Anna-Maria Żukowska": 1,
    "Katarzyna Kotula": 0.7,
    "Magdalena Biejat": 1.4
};
Q.pres_debate_rights_done = 1;
Q.pres_debate_stops_remaining -= 1;
Q.pres_debate_score += scores[Q.presidential_candidate] || 1;
Q.pres_debate_rights_line = Q.pres_debate_rights_cautious_title;
Q.psl_relation += 2;
Q.spring_dissent += 2;
Q.razem_dissent += 3;
Q.news_headline =
    Q.presidential_candidate + " narrows both rights and vaccine commitments";
!}

The commitment is real but small, and the qualifications are audible: this
much now, the rest when there is a majority for it, and on vaccination a
caution that will not be quoted approvingly by anyone.

It is the answer a campaign gives when it has decided the runoff matters more
than the first round. Whether that is a strategy or an instinct is a question
the party will be arguing about long after the count.

- @debate_economy_close: The last question and the free minute

@debate_economy_close
title: The euro and the free minute
subtitle: The final question is hypothetical; the final minute is not.
new-page: true
max-visits: 1
view-if: pres_debate_close_done = 0

Most candidates reject adopting the euro during the crisis. The studio then
grants each lectern sixty seconds on any subject. Duda asks for continuity;
Hołownia offers an escape from the old party contest. The Left can keep its
own ground or answer either man by name.

- @debate_close_social
- @debate_close_duda
- @debate_close_duopoly

@debate_close_social
title: [+ pres_debate_close_signature_title +]
subtitle: Keep the final minute on [+ presidential_candidate +]'s own political ground.
on-arrival: {!
const scores = {
    "Robert Biedroń": 2.2,
    "Adrian Zandberg": 2.8,
    "Agnieszka Dziemianowicz-Bąk": 2.5,
    "Anna-Maria Żukowska": 2.5,
    "Katarzyna Kotula": 2.5,
    "Magdalena Biejat": 2.7
};
Q.pres_debate_close_done = 1;
Q.pres_debate_stops_remaining -= 1;
Q.pres_debate_score += scores[Q.presidential_candidate] || 2.3;
Q.pres_debate_close_line = Q.pres_debate_close_signature_title;
Q.pres_debate_strategy = "Own ground";
if (Q.presidential_candidate == "Robert Biedroń") {
    Q.progressive_credibility += 2;
    Q.young_support += 1;
} else if (Q.presidential_candidate == "Adrian Zandberg") {
    Q.labor_credibility += 3;
    Q.workers_support += 1;
} else if (Q.presidential_candidate == "Agnieszka Dziemianowicz-Bąk") {
    Q.public_sector_support += 2;
    Q.labor_credibility += 2;
} else if (Q.presidential_candidate == "Anna-Maria Żukowska") {
    Q.media_capacity += 3;
} else if (Q.presidential_candidate == "Katarzyna Kotula") {
    Q.feminist_trust += 3;
    Q.women_support += 1;
} else {
    Q.household_policy_pressure += 2;
    Q.labor_credibility += 2;
}
Q.news_headline =
    Q.presidential_candidate + " uses the final minute to define the campaign";
!}

Sixty seconds, no opponent named, no institution defended. The minute is spent
describing the thing the campaign is for, in the register the candidate is
actually good in, and it ends with about four seconds unused.

Nothing about it is designed to be fair to the Left's position in the polls. It
is the only minute of the evening that belongs to us entirely, and the party
will be quoting it at doors for the rest of the month.

- @debate_verdict: The spin room

@debate_close_duda
title: [+ pres_debate_close_duda_title +]
subtitle: Reply directly to Duda; stronger democratic-camp clip, less independent ownership.
on-arrival: {!
const scores = {
    "Robert Biedroń": 2,
    "Adrian Zandberg": 2.4,
    "Agnieszka Dziemianowicz-Bąk": 2.3,
    "Anna-Maria Żukowska": 2.5,
    "Katarzyna Kotula": 2.3,
    "Magdalena Biejat": 2.2
};
Q.pres_debate_close_done = 1;
Q.pres_debate_stops_remaining -= 1;
Q.pres_debate_score += scores[Q.presidential_candidate] || 2;
Q.pres_debate_close_line = Q.pres_debate_close_duda_title;
Q.pres_debate_strategy = "Incumbent indictment";
Q.president_relation -= 3;
Q.ko_relation += 2;
Q.news_headline =
    Q.presidential_candidate + " closes with a direct answer to Duda";
!}

The free minute becomes an indictment: five years of signatures, read out with
dates, ending with the ones that were never given. The President is standing
four lecterns away and cannot answer, which is the entire construction.

By morning the clip is circulating inside the democratic camp — shared, with
approval, by people who intend to vote for [+ pres_2020_ko_surname +]. It is
the most-watched thing our campaign produces and the least likely to change
whom anyone votes for.

- @debate_verdict: The spin room

@debate_close_duopoly
title: [+ pres_debate_close_holownia_title +]
subtitle: Reply directly to Hołownia and contest his claim to political renewal.
on-arrival: {!
const scores = {
    "Robert Biedroń": 1.5,
    "Adrian Zandberg": 2.1,
    "Agnieszka Dziemianowicz-Bąk": 1.8,
    "Anna-Maria Żukowska": 2.3,
    "Katarzyna Kotula": 1.9,
    "Magdalena Biejat": 2
};
Q.pres_debate_close_done = 1;
Q.pres_debate_stops_remaining -= 1;
Q.pres_debate_score += scores[Q.presidential_candidate] || 1.6;
Q.pres_debate_close_line = Q.pres_debate_close_holownia_title;
Q.pres_debate_strategy = "Hołownia contrast";
Q.p2050_relation -= 3;
Q.media_capacity += 1;
Q.news_headline =
    Q.presidential_candidate + " answers Hołownia's claim to renewal";
!}

The minute is aimed sideways rather than upward: at the man offering an exit
from the old contest without saying who pays for the new one. It is a fair
question and an awkward one to ask, because most of the people it is aimed at
are not our voters and were never going to be.

Hołownia's volunteers take it personally. His polling does not move that night.
Ours has at least been spent on an argument nobody else in the studio was
willing to make.

- @debate_verdict: The spin room

@debate_verdict
title: The spin room
subtitle: Commit the debate result and release the final tracking poll.
new-page: true
max-visits: 1
view-if: pres_debate_stops_remaining <= 0 and pres_debate_resolved = 0
on-arrival: {!
if (!Q.pres_debate_resolved) {
    Q.pres_debate_resolved = 1;
    const isZandberg =
        Q.presidential_candidate == "Adrian Zandberg";
    const debateRoll = Number(Q.pres_debate_roll);
    Q.pres_debate_effective_score =
        (Number(Q.pres_debate_score) || 0) +
        (isZandberg ? 1.5 : 0) +
        (
            (Number.isFinite(debateRoll) ? debateRoll : 0.5) -
            0.5
        ) * 2.5 -
        (Q.hard_mode ? 0.35 : 0);

    let committedBonus = 0;
    if (Q.pres_debate_effective_score >= 6.5) {
        Q.pres_debate_outcome = "Viral upset";
        committedBonus = isZandberg ? 1.45 : 1.05;
        Q.public_trust += 4;
        Q.media_capacity += 4;
        Q.pres_turnout_bonus += 0.6;
    } else if (Q.pres_debate_effective_score >= 4.5) {
        Q.pres_debate_outcome = "Clear debate win";
        committedBonus = isZandberg ? 0.85 : 0.60;
        Q.public_trust += 2;
        Q.media_capacity += 2;
    } else if (Q.pres_debate_effective_score >= 2.5) {
        Q.pres_debate_outcome = "No clear winner";
        committedBonus = isZandberg ? 0.50 : 0.25;
    } else {
        Q.pres_debate_outcome = "Stumble";
        committedBonus = isZandberg ? 0 : -0.25;
        Q.public_trust -= 2;
        Q.media_capacity -= 1;
    }

    Q.pres_debate_committed_bonus = committedBonus;
    Q.pres_bonus_left += committedBonus;

    const strongResult =
        Q.pres_debate_outcome == "Viral upset" ||
        Q.pres_debate_outcome == "Clear debate win";
    if (strongResult &&
        Q.pres_debate_strategy == "Incumbent indictment") {
        Q.pres_bonus_duda -=
            Q.pres_debate_outcome == "Viral upset" ? 0.35 : 0.20;
    }
    if (strongResult &&
        Q.pres_debate_strategy == "Hołownia contrast") {
        Q.pres_bonus_holownia -=
            Q.pres_debate_outcome == "Viral upset" ? 0.30 : 0.18;
    }
    if (strongResult &&
        Q.pres_debate_strategy == "Own ground") {
        Q.pres_bonus_duda -= 0.10;
        Q.pres_bonus_holownia -= 0.10;
    }

    const adverseUpset =
        Q.pres_debate_outcome == "Stumble" ||
        (
            Q.pres_debate_outcome == "No clear winner" &&
            Q.pres_debate_upset_roll < 0.18
        );
    if (adverseUpset) {
        const rivalIndex =
            Q.pres_debate_outcome == "Stumble"
                ? Math.min(
                    2,
                    Math.floor(Q.pres_debate_upset_roll * 3)
                )
                : Math.min(
                    2,
                    Math.floor(Q.pres_debate_upset_roll / 0.06)
                );
        const rivalBonus =
            Q.pres_debate_outcome == "Stumble" ? 0.55 : 0.40;
        if (rivalIndex == 0) {
            Q.pres_bonus_duda += rivalBonus;
            Q.pres_debate_upset =
                "Duda's defence becomes the dominant clip";
        } else if (rivalIndex == 1) {
            Q.pres_bonus_holownia += rivalBonus;
            Q.pres_debate_upset =
                "Hołownia owns the outsider's closing minute";
        } else {
            Q.pres_bonus_bosak += rivalBonus;
            Q.pres_debate_upset =
                "Bosak's counterattack travels furthest online";
        }
    } else if (Q.pres_debate_outcome == "Viral upset") {
        Q.pres_debate_upset =
            Q.presidential_candidate +
            " breaks through the wall of eleven lecterns";
    } else {
        Q.pres_debate_upset =
            "No rival clip displaces the Left's final line";
    }

    Q.pres_first_calc_mode = "tracking_poll";
    Q.news_headline =
        Q.presidential_candidate + ": " +
        Q.pres_debate_outcome.toLowerCase() +
        " in the final television debate";
}
!}

= [+ presidential_candidate +]: [+ pres_debate_outcome +]

[? if pres_debate_outcome = "Viral upset": The spin room is a corridor with
eleven press officers in it, and by half past eleven only one of them is being
asked questions. Something in the four hours worked in a way nothing in this
campaign has worked yet: the clip is moving on its own, editors are calling the
office rather than the other way round, and people who spent the spring
explaining that a Left candidacy was symbolic are having to write a different
sentence.?]
[? if pres_debate_outcome = "Clear debate win": The verdict is reached in the
usual way — three commentators agree, and then everyone agrees. **[+
presidential_candidate +]** had the better night. It does not move the race,
because in a field of eleven nothing moves the race in one evening, but the
invitations for the last fortnight will be issued on different assumptions.?]
[? if pres_debate_outcome = "No clear winner": Eleven lecterns, five questions
and a free minute, and the honest verdict is that everyone left the studio with
what they brought into it. There are three usable lines in the recording. There
is no moment large enough to reorder anything.?]
[? if pres_debate_outcome = "Stumble": It went badly and everyone in the
corridor knows it went badly. One answer arrived a beat late, one arrived
without an ending, and the format punished both. The press officers do the
thing press officers do, which is to talk about the questions rather than the
answers.?]

[+ pres_debate_upset +].

**The argument the audience heard**

**Opening questions:** [+ pres_debate_frame_line +]

**Rights and public health:** [+ pres_debate_rights_line +]

**Final minute:** [+ pres_debate_close_line +]

[? if presidential_candidate = "Robert Biedroń" and pres_debate_outcome = "No clear winner":
The result resembles the historical night: clear positions, several usable
lines and no single moment large enough to reorder the field.?]

[? if presidential_candidate = "Adrian Zandberg": The candidate's earlier
national-debate experience raises both the floor and the ceiling of the
performance.?]

