@left_frame
title: What kind of runoff coalition?
new-page: true

The Left's candidate has reached the runoff but still needs voters from outside
the party. Choose whether to build the campaign around democratic cooperation,
class conflict, or equality and civil rights.

- @left_frame_social
- @left_frame_class
- @left_frame_equality

@left_frame_social
title: A democratic-social presidency
subtitle: Best bridge to KO and Hołownia; the platform retains a social floor.
on-arrival: {!
Q.pres_runoff_endorsement = "Own candidacy";
Q.pres_runoff_campaign = "Democratic-social coalition";
Q.pres_runoff_target_bonus += 0.62;
Q.pres_runoff_preparation += 0.45;
Q.ko_relation += 4;
Q.p2050_relation += 3;
Q.labor_credibility += 2;
Q.news_headline =
    Q.presidential_candidate +
    " assembles a democratic-social runoff front";
!}

The campaign is rebuilt in four days around a proposition that KO's voters and
Hołownia's can both accept without being asked to become socialists: courts,
appointments and a signature that will not be used against them, plus a social
floor that stays in the text rather than in the speeches.

It is the version of the candidacy most likely to win and least likely to be
recognisable to the people who nominated it. Both facts are understood in the
room, and the decision is taken anyway.

- @support_market: Open the inter-round support market

@left_frame_class
title: A revolt of wage earners against both old camps
subtitle: Strong mobilisation; much harder trades with KO and PSL.
on-arrival: {!
Q.pres_runoff_endorsement = "Own candidacy";
Q.pres_runoff_campaign = "Class insurgency";
Q.pres_runoff_target_bonus += 0.78;
Q.workers_support += 3;
Q.labor_credibility += 4;
Q.razem_dissent -= 5;
Q.ko_relation -= 5;
Q.psl_relation -= 3;
Q.news_headline =
    Q.presidential_candidate + " turns the runoff into a class contest";
!}

The runoff is fought as a wage argument. Not a defence of the constitution
against PiS, not a modernisation offer against the countryside — a straight
claim that both old camps have spent thirty years agreeing about who pays, and
that the ballot is the first chance in a decade to make them stop.

Turnout in the places the campaign is aimed at goes up. So does the number of
KO mayors and PSL county chairs who conclude that there is nothing here for
them to work with, which in a two-week campaign is a serious quantity of doors
that will not be knocked.

- @support_market: Open the inter-round support market

@left_frame_equality
title: A republic of equal citizens
subtitle: Women and young voters lead; conservative caucuses may refuse the field work.
on-arrival: {!
Q.pres_runoff_endorsement = "Own candidacy";
Q.pres_runoff_campaign = "Equality republic";
Q.pres_runoff_target_bonus += 0.70;
Q.feminist_trust += 5;
Q.women_support += 3;
Q.young_support += 2;
Q.barons_dissent += 6;
Q.psl_relation -= 2;
Q.news_headline =
    Q.presidential_candidate + " makes equality the runoff dividing line";
!}

The fortnight is fought on citizenship: who is counted, whose family is
recognised, whose safety is treated as a policy question rather than a
provocation. It is the argument the campaign has been having with the country
since the autumn, made at last with a ballot attached.

Young voters and women in the cities respond in numbers the party has no
recent precedent for. Three regional organisations decline to run the
door-knocking, and one of them says why on the record.

- @support_market: Open the inter-round support market

@endorsement
title: The Left's endorsement
new-page: true

The default democratic option is **[+ pres_runoff_support_name +]**. An
endorsement changes only the transfer probability of Left voters.

- @endorse_accord
- @endorse_immediate
- @endorse_free
- @endorse_duda_deal

@endorse_accord
title: Trade the endorsement for a written social and constitutional accord
subtitle: Cost: 2 resources. Requires a democratic finalist willing to bargain.
choose-if: resources >= 2 and pres_runoff_target_relation >= 35 and pres_runoff_support_key != "duda" and pres_runoff_support_key != "bosak"
unavailable-subtitle: The target will not pay this policy price, or the Left cannot finance joint mobilisation.
on-arrival: resources -= 2; pres_runoff_endorsement = "Negotiated social-constitutional accord"; pres_runoff_target_bonus += 0.30; pres_runoff_preparation += 0.55; party_unity += 2; labor_credibility += 2; progressive_credibility += 2; ko_relation += 4 if pres_runoff_support_key = "trzaskowski"; p2050_relation += 4 if pres_runoff_support_key = "holownia"; psl_relation += 4 if pres_runoff_support_key = "kosiniak"; news_headline = "The Left prices its runoff endorsement"

Three days of talks in a building nobody photographs, and a text at the end of
them: named commitments on health and labour law, a standard for judicial
appointments, and a promise about which bills reach the desk first. **[+
pres_runoff_support_name +]** signs it because a fortnight is very short.

The document is not enforceable and everyone signing it knows so. Its value is
that it is public: a broken clause becomes a story rather than a private
disappointment, and our own people have something to campaign for rather than
merely against.

- @support_market: Open the inter-round support market

@endorse_immediate
title: Endorse the democratic finalist without conditions
subtitle: Better voter compliance; no enforceable programme.
choose-if: pres_runoff_support_key != "bosak"
unavailable-subtitle: The leadership will not present a radical-right endorsement as democratic unity.
on-arrival: {!
Q.pres_runoff_endorsement = "Immediate lesser-evil endorsement";
Q.pres_runoff_target_bonus += 0.12;
Q.pres_runoff_preparation += 0.18;
Q.public_trust += 1;
Q.razem_dissent += 4;
if (Q.pres_runoff_support_key == "trzaskowski") Q.ko_relation += 4;
if (Q.pres_runoff_support_key == "holownia") Q.p2050_relation += 4;
if (Q.pres_runoff_support_key == "kosiniak") Q.psl_relation += 4;
Q.news_headline = "The Left endorses " + Q.pres_runoff_support_name;
!}

The statement goes out on Monday morning without conditions attached, because
the leadership has decided that the difference between the two remaining
presidencies is too large to be used as leverage.

It is the honest version and the cheap one. **[+ pres_runoff_support_name +]**'s
staff are grateful for about a day, and by Wednesday nobody in that building
is being asked what the Left was promised, because the answer is nothing.

- @support_market: Open the inter-round support market

@endorse_free
title: Release Left voters without an endorsement
subtitle: Preserves autonomy; depresses transfer and angers the democratic camp.
on-arrival: pres_runoff_endorsement = "Free vote"; ko_relation -= 8 if pres_runoff_support_key = "trzaskowski"; p2050_relation -= 5 if pres_runoff_support_key = "holownia"; party_unity -= 2; progressives_dissent += 5; spring_dissent += 5; razem_dissent -= 2; news_headline = "The Left refuses to command its runoff voters"

The wording takes an afternoon to agree and says, in the end, that our voters
are adults, that neither finalist asked us for anything, and that the party will
not spend its remaining authority instructing people it could not persuade to
turn out in the first place.

The democratic camp treats this as sabotage and says so in every studio for a
week. Inside the party the same decision is read as the first honest thing the
leadership has done since the nomination, which tells you how far apart those
two rooms now are.

- @support_market: Open the inter-round support market

@endorse_duda_deal
title: Offer Duda a welfare and institutional non-aggression pact
subtitle: Palace path: a large internal rupture for a narrow written price.
view-if: pres_finalist_a_key = "duda" or pres_finalist_b_key = "duda"
choose-if: president_relation >= 30 or presidential_channel_open = 1 or pis_relation >= 20
unavailable-subtitle: The Palace has no trusted channel to the Left.
on-arrival: pres_runoff_support_key = "duda"; pres_runoff_support_name = "Andrzej Duda"; pres_runoff_endorsement = "Palace welfare deal"; pres_runoff_target_bonus += 0.16; president_relation += 10; pis_relation += 4; ko_relation -= 14; razem_dissent += 15; progressives_dissent += 12; spring_dissent += 10; barons_dissent -= 5; party_unity -= 8; news_headline = "A Left–Palace runoff pact shocks both camps"

What is agreed is narrow and written down: the transfers are not touched, the
pension indexation stands, two named appointments are consulted, and the Palace
will not use the campaign against us. What is given is the one thing the Left
has left, which is permission.

The reaction is not a debate. Razem's council meets the same evening; two Wiosna
MPs release a statement before it finishes; the equality organisations that
staffed the spring stop answering the phone entirely. Whatever the pact is
worth on the count, the party that signed it will not be the same party
afterwards.

- @support_market: Open the inter-round support market

@support_market
title: Inter-round support market
new-page: true

= Two negotiations — [+ pres_support_actions_remaining +] remain

Our line is **[+ pres_runoff_endorsement +]**, and the campaign we are asking
our voters to reach is **[+ pres_runoff_support_name +]**. That much is
published. What remains is the part nobody reports: fourteen days in which
several million people whose candidate is no longer on the ballot decide
whether to vote at all.

The Left can broker, mobilise or persuade. Every deal changes one eliminated
electorate or creates new turnout; it does not transfer an entire party.

- @support_holownia
- @support_psl
- @support_ko
- @support_movements
- @support_bosak
- @support_turnout
- @support_release

@support_holownia
title: Offer Hołownia an oversight and public-service accord
subtitle: Cost: 1 resource. Better with an existing Poland 2050 relationship.
view-if: pres_support_holownia = 0 and pres_finalist_a_key != "holownia" and pres_finalist_b_key != "holownia"
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: No shared operation can be staffed.
on-arrival: {!
Q.resources -= 1;
Q.pres_support_holownia = 1;
Q.pres_support_actions_remaining -= 1;
Q.pres_trade_holownia_boost =
    0.055 + (Q.p2050_relation >= 35 ? 0.035 : 0);
Q.p2050_relation += 4;
Q.pres_runoff_target_bonus += 0.10;
Q.news_headline =
    "Hołownia's camp offers conditional runoff cooperation";
!}

Hołownia's people begin by explaining that they cannot deliver anybody, which
is true and also the most useful thing they say. What they can deliver is a
joint text on parliamentary oversight and a commitment about the public
services their volunteers spent the spring talking about.

It is published under both names. His electorate is the least tribal in the
country and the most likely to respond to being given a reason rather than an
instruction — and the least likely to forgive either camp for treating it as
property.

- @support_next
- @support_done

@support_psl
title: Give PSL a county-services and local-autonomy guarantee
subtitle: Cost: 1 resource. A rural bridge with a conservative policy edge.
view-if: pres_support_psl = 0 and pres_finalist_a_key != "kosiniak" and pres_finalist_b_key != "kosiniak"
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: PSL will not trade on an unfunded promise.
on-arrival: {!
Q.resources -= 1;
Q.pres_support_psl = 1;
Q.pres_support_actions_remaining -= 1;
Q.pres_trade_psl_boost =
    0.06 + (Q.psl_relation >= 35 ? 0.035 : 0);
Q.psl_relation += 5;
Q.local_network += 2;
Q.rural_support += 2;
Q.progressives_dissent += 2;
Q.news_headline = "PSL prices its county networks";
!}

PSL does not negotiate about the presidency. It negotiates about bus routes,
county hospitals and who decides what happens to a school when there are
eleven children left in it. The guarantee is written in that language because
that is the only language in which it will be believed.

The mayors it reaches are a genuine asset in places the Left has never won
anything. The price is a paragraph about local autonomy that our own
progressive organisations read twice and do not like.

- @support_next
- @support_done

@support_ko
title: Exchange constitutional guarantees for KO's full field operation
subtitle: Cost: 2 resources. Available only when KO's candidate is eliminated.
view-if: pres_support_ko = 0 and pres_finalist_a_key != "trzaskowski" and pres_finalist_b_key != "trzaskowski" and pres_runoff_support_key != "duda" and pres_runoff_support_key != "bosak"
choose-if: resources >= 2 and ko_relation >= 45
unavailable-subtitle: KO lacks trust in the target or the operation cannot be financed.
on-arrival: resources -= 2; pres_support_ko = 1; pres_support_actions_remaining -= 1; pres_trade_ko_boost = 0.11; ko_relation += 6; constitutional_restraint += 3; razem_dissent += 4; pres_runoff_target_bonus += 0.22; news_headline = "KO opens its municipal machine to the runoff target"

With their own candidate eliminated, KO has a machine and nothing to spend it
on. What they want for it is written into a single page about the courts, the
appointments and the limits of the office — the guarantees a liberal party
requires before it lends its city halls to somebody else.

It is the largest field operation available anywhere in the country and it
arrives fully staffed. Razem's organisers, watching the same city halls that
spent five years explaining why the Left was unnecessary, need some persuading
that this is a victory.

- @support_next
- @support_done

@support_movements
title: Activate union, feminist and tenant turnout committees
subtitle: No party transfer. Works only for a democratic or Left target.
view-if: pres_support_movements = 0
choose-if: pres_runoff_support_key != "duda" and pres_runoff_support_key != "bosak"
unavailable-subtitle: The movements refuse the selected endorsement.
on-arrival: pres_support_movements = 1; pres_support_actions_remaining -= 1; pres_trade_left_boost += 0.055; pres_runoff_target_bonus += 0.62; organiser_energy -= 4; turnout_readiness += 2; feminist_trust += 2; labor_credibility += 2; news_headline = "Independent movements build a runoff turnout operation"

It is not run from party headquarters and it does not carry the party's name.
Three union federations, the tenants' associations and the women's
organisations put a committee together whose only purpose is getting people to
a polling station in the middle of a pandemic.

They can knock on the doors of people who despise parties and be believed. The
cost is that our offices are empty for a fortnight and the organisers who do
this work will be finished for a month afterwards.

- @support_next
- @support_done

@support_bosak
title: Contest Bosak's voters on wages, privacy and anti-duopoly anger
subtitle: No leadership endorsement; a risky appeal to an eliminated electorate.
view-if: pres_support_bosak = 0 and pres_finalist_a_key != "bosak" and pres_finalist_b_key != "bosak"
on-arrival: pres_support_bosak = 1; pres_support_actions_remaining -= 1; pres_trade_bosak_boost = 0.045; labor_credibility += 1; minority_safety -= 3; progressive_credibility -= 3; progressives_dissent += 4; news_headline = "The runoff campaign contests rather than endorses the radical-right electorate"

Nothing is offered to Bosak and nothing is asked of him. The argument is made
past him, to the twenty-year-olds who voted for him because their wages are
low, their landlord is unaccountable and the state has spent their adult lives
telling them what to do without telling them anything true.

A few of them listen. The rest of the fortnight is spent explaining, to our own
members and to two national newspapers, why a Left campaign is holding meetings
in that vocabulary at all — and the explanation does not fully survive contact
with the people who have to hear it.

- @support_next
- @support_done

@support_turnout
title: Spend the negotiation on registration, rides and ballot protection
subtitle: Free fallback. Creates turnout instead of claiming another party.
view-if: pres_support_turnout = 0
on-arrival: pres_support_turnout = 1; pres_support_actions_remaining -= 1; pres_runoff_target_bonus += 0.38; pres_turnout_bonus += 0.7; turnout_readiness += 2; local_network += 1; news_headline = "The Left turns one bargaining slot into turnout"

Certificates for people voting away from home, transport in counties where the
polling station is nine kilometres from the estate, and an observer in every
precinct where the May postal fiasco left a protocol somebody had to correct.

Nobody is negotiated with and nobody is thanked. It is the least interesting
item on the board, and in a runoff decided by a point it is the item least
likely to have been wasted.

- @support_next
- @support_done

@support_release
title: Keep one slot empty and let every organisation decide
subtitle: Guaranteed fallback. No transfer bonus; less factional ownership of the result.
view-if: pres_support_release = 0
on-arrival: pres_support_release = 1; pres_support_actions_remaining -= 1; party_unity += 1; movement_autonomy += 2; news_headline = "The Left closes one runoff negotiation without a deal"

The meeting takes place and produces nothing, which is a decision rather than a
failure. Every organisation in the room keeps its own line and the party keeps
the ability to say afterwards that it promised no one anything.

In a fortnight where every camp is acquiring debts, declining one is worth
something to the people who will have to live in this party in July. It is
worth nothing whatsoever on the count.

- @support_next
- @support_done

@support_next
title: Return to the support market
view-if: pres_support_actions_remaining > 0
go-to: support_market

@support_done
title: Close the negotiations and read the runoff poll
view-if: pres_support_actions_remaining <= 0
go-to: runoff_poll

@calculate_runoff
on-arrival: {!
const clampRunoff = function(value, low, high) {
    return Math.max(low, Math.min(high, Number(value) || 0));
};
const sources = [
    "duda", "trzaskowski", "holownia", "bosak",
    "kosiniak", "left", "other"
];
const positions = {
    left: -0.85,
    trzaskowski: -0.25,
    holownia: 0.05,
    other: 0.10,
    kosiniak: 0.25,
    duda: 0.72,
    bosak: 0.95
};
const sourceShares = {};
for (const source of sources) {
    sourceShares[source] =
        Math.max(0, Number(Q["pres_r1_raw_" + source]) || 0);
}
const a = Q.pres_finalist_a_key;
const b = Q.pres_finalist_b_key;
const target = Q.pres_runoff_support_key;
const commonDudaTrz =
    (a == "duda" && b == "trzaskowski") ||
    (a == "trzaskowski" && b == "duda");
const leftDuda =
    (a == "left" && b == "duda") ||
    (a == "duda" && b == "left");
const vectorFor = function(source) {
    if (source == a) return {a: 0.985, b: 0, abstain: 0.015};
    if (source == b) return {a: 0, b: 0.985, abstain: 0.015};
    const orient = function(firstKey, first, secondKey, second, abstain) {
        const vector = {a: 0, b: 0, abstain: abstain};
        if (a == firstKey) vector.a = first;
        if (b == firstKey) vector.b = first;
        if (a == secondKey) vector.a = second;
        if (b == secondKey) vector.b = second;
        return vector;
    };
    if (commonDudaTrz) {
        if (source == "holownia") {
            const breakoutAbstention = Q.pres_breakout_key == "holownia"
                ? Math.min(0.20, (Number(Q.pres_breakout_size) || 0) * 0.01)
                : 0;
            return orient(
                "duda",
                0.14,
                "trzaskowski",
                0.76 - breakoutAbstention,
                0.10 + breakoutAbstention
            );
        }
        if (source == "kosiniak") {
            return orient("duda", 0.24, "trzaskowski", 0.64, 0.12);
        }
        if (source == "bosak") {
            return orient("duda", 0.54, "trzaskowski", 0.27, 0.19);
        }
        if (source == "left") {
            return orient("duda", 0.04, "trzaskowski", 0.67, 0.29);
        }
        return orient("duda", 0.24, "trzaskowski", 0.45, 0.31);
    }
    if (leftDuda) {
        if (source == "holownia") {
            return orient("duda", 0.25, "left", 0.65, 0.10);
        }
        if (source == "kosiniak") {
            return orient("duda", 0.43, "left", 0.45, 0.12);
        }
        if (source == "bosak") {
            return orient("duda", 0.55, "left", 0.20, 0.25);
        }
        if (source == "trzaskowski") {
            return orient("duda", 0.07, "left", 0.83, 0.10);
        }
        return orient("duda", 0.25, "left", 0.50, 0.25);
    }
    const distanceA = Math.abs(positions[source] - positions[a]);
    const distanceB = Math.abs(positions[source] - positions[b]);
    const turnoutBySource = {
        duda: 0.985,
        trzaskowski: 0.94,
        holownia: 0.88,
        bosak: 0.78,
        kosiniak: 0.86,
        left: 0.84,
        other: 0.72
    };
    const active = turnoutBySource[source] || 0.8;
    const aPreference =
        1 / (1 + Math.exp((distanceA - distanceB) * 3.0));
    return {
        a: active * aPreference,
        b: active * (1 - aPreference),
        abstain: 1 - active
    };
};
const boostToward = function(vector, candidate, amount) {
    if (candidate != a && candidate != b) return vector;
    const targetField = candidate == a ? "a" : "b";
    const otherField = candidate == a ? "b" : "a";
    const room = Math.max(0, 1 - vector[targetField]);
    let shift = Math.min(Math.max(0, amount), room);
    let fromAbstain = Math.min(vector.abstain, shift * 0.70);
    vector.abstain -= fromAbstain;
    vector[targetField] += fromAbstain;
    shift -= fromAbstain;
    const fromOther = Math.min(vector[otherField], shift);
    vector[otherField] -= fromOther;
    vector[targetField] += fromOther;
    shift -= fromOther;
    if (shift > 0) {
        const lastAbstain = Math.min(vector.abstain, shift);
        vector.abstain -= lastAbstain;
        vector[targetField] += lastAbstain;
    }
    const total = vector.a + vector.b + vector.abstain;
    vector.abstain += 1 - total;
    return vector;
};

// A runoff that puts the incumbent against a challenger from outside the
// democratic camp is partly a referendum on five years of PiS. Where trust has
// collapsed, part of the eliminated electorate votes against Duda whoever the
// alternative is, instead of staying at home.
const dudaReferendum =
    !commonDudaTrz && !leftDuda && (a == "duda" || b == "duda");
const dudaChallenger = a == "duda" ? b : a;
const antiIncumbentPull = clampRunoff(
    0.10 +
        (45 - (Number(Q.public_trust) || 43)) * 0.010 +
        ((Number(Q.far_right_agenda) || 32) - 32) * 0.004,
    0,
    0.55
);

let rawA = 0;
let rawB = 0;
let abstentionRaw = 0;
for (const source of sources) {
    let vector = vectorFor(source);
    if (source == "left" && source != a && source != b) {
        let endorsementBoost = 0;
        if (Q.pres_runoff_endorsement ==
            "Negotiated social-constitutional accord") {
            endorsementBoost = 0.16;
        } else if (Q.pres_runoff_endorsement ==
            "Immediate lesser-evil endorsement") {
            endorsementBoost = 0.09;
        } else if (Q.pres_runoff_endorsement ==
            "Palace welfare deal") {
            endorsementBoost = 0.30;
        }
        endorsementBoost += Number(Q.pres_trade_left_boost) || 0;
        vector = boostToward(vector, target, endorsementBoost);
        if (commonDudaTrz) {
            const razemShare = clampRunoff(
                (Number(Q.razem_strength) || 20) / 100,
                0.05,
                0.45
            );
            const promisesSecured = Q.pres_runoff_endorsement ==
                "Negotiated social-constitutional accord";
            const razemStayHomeRate = promisesSecured
                ? 0.20
                : clampRunoff(
                    0.50 +
                        ((Number(Q.razem_dissent) || 20) - 20) * 0.004,
                    0.50,
                    0.70
                );
            const active = vector.a + vector.b;
            const stranded = Math.min(
                active,
                razemShare * razemStayHomeRate
            );
            if (active > 0) {
                vector.a -= stranded * vector.a / active;
                vector.b -= stranded * vector.b / active;
                vector.abstain += stranded;
            }
            Q.pres_razem_trzaskowski_reluctance =
                Math.round(razemStayHomeRate * 1000) / 10;
        }
    }
    if (source == "holownia" && source != a && source != b) {
        vector = boostToward(
            vector,
            target,
            Number(Q.pres_trade_holownia_boost) || 0
        );
    }
    if (source == "kosiniak" && source != a && source != b) {
        vector = boostToward(
            vector,
            target,
            Number(Q.pres_trade_psl_boost) || 0
        );
    }
    if (source == "trzaskowski" && source != a && source != b) {
        vector = boostToward(
            vector,
            target,
            Number(Q.pres_trade_ko_boost) || 0
        );
    }
    if (source == "bosak" && source != a && source != b) {
        vector = boostToward(
            vector,
            target,
            Number(Q.pres_trade_bosak_boost) || 0
        );
    }
    if (dudaReferendum && source != "duda" && source != dudaChallenger) {
        vector = boostToward(vector, dudaChallenger, antiIncumbentPull);
    }
    const sourceShare = sourceShares[source];
    rawA += sourceShare * vector.a;
    rawB += sourceShare * vector.b;
    abstentionRaw += sourceShare * vector.abstain;
    const targetShare = target == a ? vector.a :
        (target == b ? vector.b : 0);
    if (source == "left") {
        Q.pres_transfer_left_target =
            Math.round(targetShare * 1000) / 10;
    }
    if (source == "holownia") {
        Q.pres_transfer_holownia_target =
            Math.round(targetShare * 1000) / 10;
    }
    if (source == "kosiniak") {
        Q.pres_transfer_psl_target =
            Math.round(targetShare * 1000) / 10;
    }
    if (source == "trzaskowski") {
        Q.pres_transfer_ko_target =
            Math.round(targetShare * 1000) / 10;
    }
    if (source == "bosak") {
        Q.pres_transfer_bosak_target =
            Math.round(targetShare * 1000) / 10;
    }
    if (source == "other") {
        Q.pres_transfer_other_target =
            Math.round(targetShare * 1000) / 10;
    }
}
Q.pres_transfer_abstention =
    Math.round(abstentionRaw * 100) / 100;

const newTurnout = {
    // The incumbent starts favoured; only a full inter-round operation closes it.
    duda: 5.20,
    trzaskowski: 1.10,
    holownia: 1.35,
    bosak: 0.90,
    kosiniak: 0.75,
    left: 1.60 + (Q.pres_ko_joint_candidate ? 1.40 : 0),
    other: 0
};
rawA += newTurnout[a] || 0;
rawB += newTurnout[b] || 0;
// The Left can spend its whole machine on another finalist, but it cannot add
// the weight of a major-party campaign unless it earned that weight in round
// one. Transfer deals above still move the electorates they actually address.
const targetLeverage = target == "left"
    ? 1
    : clampRunoff(sourceShares.left / 10, 0.25, 0.85);
Q.pres_runoff_target_leverage =
    Math.round(targetLeverage * 100) / 100;
const targetBonus = (
    (Number(Q.pres_runoff_target_bonus) || 0) +
    (Number(Q.pres_runoff_preparation) || 0) * 0.35
) * targetLeverage;
if (target == a) rawA += targetBonus;
if (target == b) rawB += targetBonus;

const shock = Q.pres_runoff_calc_mode == "result"
    ? Number(Q.pres_runoff_result_shock) || 0
    : Number(Q.pres_runoff_poll_shock) || 0;
rawA = Math.max(0.1, rawA + shock);
rawB = Math.max(0.1, rawB - shock);
const validRaw = rawA + rawB;
const shareA = rawA * 100 / Math.max(0.1, validRaw);
const shareB = 100 - shareA;
const displayA = Math.round(shareA * 10) / 10;
const displayB = Math.round((100 - displayA) * 10) / 10;

if (Q.pres_runoff_calc_mode == "poll") {
    Q.pres_runoff_poll_a = displayA;
    Q.pres_runoff_poll_b = displayB;
}
if (Q.pres_runoff_calc_mode == "result") {
    const wasNewRunoff = !Q.pres_runoff_complete;
    Q.pres_runoff_raw_a = shareA;
    Q.pres_runoff_raw_b = shareB;
    Q.pres_runoff_display_a = displayA;
    Q.pres_runoff_display_b = displayB;
    const turnout = clampRunoff(
        68.18 +
            ((Number(Q.turnout_readiness) || 58) - 58) * 0.030 +
            (Number(Q.pres_turnout_bonus) || 0) * 0.12 -
            abstentionRaw * 0.018 +
            (Number(Q.pres_runoff_turnout_shock) || 0),
        58,
        76
    );
    Q.pres_runoff_turnout = Math.round(turnout * 100) / 100;
    Q.pres_runoff_valid_votes = Math.round(
        20458911 * turnout / 68.18
    );
    Q.pres_runoff_votes_a = Math.floor(
        Q.pres_runoff_valid_votes * shareA / 100
    );
    Q.pres_runoff_votes_b =
        Q.pres_runoff_valid_votes - Q.pres_runoff_votes_a;
    const formatVotes = function(value) {
        return String(Math.round(value)).replace(
            /\B(?=(\d{3})+(?!\d))/g,
            " "
        );
    };
    Q.pres_runoff_votes_a_display =
        formatVotes(Q.pres_runoff_votes_a);
    Q.pres_runoff_votes_b_display =
        formatVotes(Q.pres_runoff_votes_b);
    Q.pres_runoff_valid_votes_display =
        formatVotes(Q.pres_runoff_valid_votes);
    const rankedKey = shareA > shareB ? a : b;
    // The KO row keeps its internal key through the transfer model, but only
    // an actual Trzaskowski presidency may enter the Trzaskowski chapter.
    const winnerKey =
        rankedKey == "trzaskowski" && Q.pres_2020_ko_kidawa
            ? "kidawa"
            : rankedKey;
    const winnerName = shareA > shareB
        ? Q.pres_finalist_a_name
        : Q.pres_finalist_b_name;
    Q.pres_runoff_winner_key = winnerKey;
    Q.pres_runoff_winner_name = winnerName;
    const presWinnerImages2020 = {
        "Andrzej Duda": "img/poland/events/pres-candidate-duda-2020.webp",
        "Rafał Trzaskowski": "img/poland/events/pres-candidate-trzaskowski.webp",
        "Małgorzata Kidawa-Błońska": "img/poland/events/pres-candidate-kidawa-2020.webp",
        "Szymon Hołownia": "img/poland/events/pres-candidate-holownia-2020.webp",
        "Krzysztof Bosak": "img/poland/events/pres-candidate-bosak.webp",
        "Władysław Kosiniak-Kamysz": "img/poland/events/pres-candidate-kosiniak-2020.webp",
        "Robert Biedroń": "img/poland/events/pres-candidate-biedron-2020.webp",
        "Adrian Zandberg": "img/poland/events/adrian-zandberg-2020.webp",
        "Agnieszka Dziemianowicz-Bąk": "img/poland/cards/advisor-dziemianowicz-bak.webp",
        "Anna-Maria Żukowska": "img/poland/cards/advisor-zukowska.webp",
        "Katarzyna Kotula": "img/poland/cards/advisor-kotula.webp",
        "Magdalena Biejat": "img/poland/cards/advisor-biejat.webp"
    };
    this.game.scenes[
        "poland_presidential_election.runoff_count"
    ].faceImage = winnerKey == "duda" || winnerKey == "bosak"
        ? "img/poland/events/wajda.jpg"
        : presWinnerImages2020[winnerName] ||
            "img/poland/events/presidential-ballot-2020.webp";
    Q.pres_runoff_margin =
        Math.round(Math.abs(shareA - shareB) * 100) / 100;
    Q.pres_2020_president_elect_key = winnerKey;
    Q.pres_2020_president_elect_name = winnerName;
    Q.president_name = "Andrzej Duda";
    Q.trzaskowski_won = winnerKey == "trzaskowski" ? 1 : 0;
    Q.left_president = 0;
    if (wasNewRunoff) {
        if (winnerKey == "trzaskowski" || winnerKey == "kidawa") {
            Q.president_relation = Math.max(
                Number(Q.president_relation) || 0,
                Q.pres_runoff_support_key == "trzaskowski" ? 58 : 48
            );
            Q.ko_relation += 5;
            if (winnerKey == "trzaskowski") {
                Q.trz_inauguration_status =
                    "President-elect — certification pending";
            }
        } else if (winnerKey == "left") {
            Q.president_relation = 82;
            Q.party_unity += 8;
            Q.public_trust += 5;
            // The ordinary first-round call is replaced by the alignment-gated
            // presidential-victory payoff on this route.
            Q.kwasniewski_2020_done = 1;
        } else if (winnerKey == "duda") {
            Q.president_relation +=
                Q.pres_runoff_support_key == "duda" ? 8 : -4;
        } else {
            Q.president_relation = 45;
        }
    }
    Q.pres_runoff_complete = 1;
    Q.pres_2020_active = 0;
    Q.pres_2020_phase = winnerKey == "trzaskowski"
        ? "Certification pending"
        : (winnerKey == "duda" ? "Election complete" : "Oath pending");
    Q.news_headline = winnerName +
        " wins the presidency by " + Q.pres_runoff_margin + " points";
    const presidentialRunoffModel = (typeof window !== "undefined"
        ? window : globalThis).polandElectionModel;
    const familyForFinalist = function(id) {
        return {
            duda: "pis", trzaskowski: "ko", kidawa: "ko",
            holownia: "p2050", bosak: "konf", kosiniak: "psl",
            left: "left", other: "other"
        }[id] || "other";
    };
    presidentialRunoffModel.archivePresident(Q,
        presidentialRunoffModel.allocatePresident({
            state: Q,
            key: "2020-07-r2",
            label: "2020 presidential election — runoff",
            round: 2,
            candidates: [
                {id: a, name: Q.pres_finalist_a_name,
                    family: familyForFinalist(a), share: shareA},
                {id: b, name: Q.pres_finalist_b_name,
                    family: familyForFinalist(b), share: shareB}
            ]
        })
    );
}
!}

@runoff_poll
title: The runoff tracking poll
new-page: true
on-arrival: pres_runoff_calc_mode = "poll"
call: poland_presidential_election.calculate_runoff

= The campaign between ballots

Poll margin: **±1.8 points**. First-round voters are not owned by the candidates
they supported. The finalists must keep their own coalitions while persuading
people whose preferred name is no longer on the ballot.

<div class="poll-table">
<div class="poll-row"><span><b>[+ pres_finalist_a_name +]</b></span><span>[+ pres_runoff_poll_a +]%</span><span>finalist A</span></div>
<div class="poll-row"><span><b>[+ pres_finalist_b_name +]</b></span><span>[+ pres_runoff_poll_b +]%</span><span>finalist B</span></div>
</div>

We are asking our voters to support **[+ pres_runoff_support_name +]** under
**[+ pres_runoff_endorsement +]**. [? if pres_finalist_a_key = "trzaskowski" or
pres_finalist_b_key = "trzaskowski": Razem organisers remain reluctant to
campaign for [+ pres_2020_ko_surname +].[? if pres_runoff_endorsement !=
"Negotiated social-constitutional accord": Without written promises, **[+
pres_razem_trzaskowski_reluctance +]%** of Razem-leaning first-round voters are
expected to stay home rather than vote for either finalist.?]?] Hołownia's volunteers, PSL's local networks and Bosak's
anti-system electorate are making their own choices too.

- @final_push_safe
- @final_push_ground
- @final_push_gamble

@final_push_safe
title: Protect the agreements and make no final promise
subtitle: Small disciplined gain; lowest factional risk.
on-arrival: pres_runoff_final_push = "Held the line"; pres_runoff_target_bonus += 0.15; party_unity += 1; pres_runoff_calc_mode = "result"; news_headline = "The runoff closes on the negotiated coalition"

Nothing new is offered, leaked or improved upon. Every appearance repeats the
text already agreed, every organiser works the list already drawn, and the
leadership spends the last week declining to make commitments under pressure
from people who will not have to keep them.

It is the least interesting fortnight available. It is also the only one that
leaves no debts behind on the Monday morning.

- @runoff_count: Open the second ballot

@final_push_ground
title: Put every remaining organiser on election-day turnout
subtitle: Stronger target mobilisation; organisers will be exhausted.
on-arrival: pres_runoff_final_push = "Ground operation"; pres_runoff_target_bonus += 0.48; pres_turnout_bonus += 0.45; organiser_energy -= 5; turnout_readiness += 1; pres_runoff_calc_mode = "result"; news_headline = "The Left empties its offices into the runoff ground game"

Every district office becomes a phone bank. Regional staff sleep on floors, the
youth organisation runs the transport, and the entire apparatus spends the last
week on the one thing that cannot be bought late: reminding people who already
agree with us that the date is Sunday.

There will be nobody left standing in this party capable of organising anything
for a month afterwards. That is a problem for August.

- @runoff_count: Open the second ballot

@final_push_gamble
title: Release an aggressive final digital contrast
subtitle: High reach and greater backlash inside a fragile alliance.
on-arrival: pres_runoff_final_push = "Final contrast"; pres_runoff_target_bonus += 0.62; media_capacity += 1; public_trust -= 1; party_unity -= 2; pres_runoff_calc_mode = "result"; news_headline = "A final contrast ad dominates the runoff silence"

The material is accurate, unpleasant and everywhere: what the other finalist
signed, said, promised and abandoned, cut to fifteen seconds and pushed into
every feed the budget can reach, right up to the electoral silence.

It does not persuade anybody. It makes the alternative unbearable to a few
hundred thousand people who would otherwise have stayed at home, which in a
runoff is the same thing. Two of our own MPs decline to share it, and the
complaint is not that it is untrue.

- @runoff_count: Open the second ballot

@runoff_count
title: Presidential runoff count
face-image: img/poland/events/presidential-ballot-2020.webp
new-page: true
call: poland_presidential_election.calculate_runoff

= [+ pres_runoff_winner_name +] elected President

Turnout: **[+ pres_runoff_turnout +]%**  
Valid votes: **[+ pres_runoff_valid_votes_display +]**

<div class="poll-table">
<div class="poll-row"><span><b>[+ pres_finalist_a_name +]</b></span><span>[+ pres_runoff_display_a +]%</span><span>[+ pres_runoff_votes_a_display +]</span></div>
<div class="poll-row"><span><b>[+ pres_finalist_b_name +]</b></span><span>[+ pres_runoff_display_b +]%</span><span>[+ pres_runoff_votes_b_display +]</span></div>
</div>

{!<div class="election-map-host" data-election-map-source="president-2020-r2"></div>!}

The margin is **[+ pres_runoff_margin +] points**. The result came from retained
first-round votes, partial transfers, abstention and new turnout—not from a
single endorsement switch. Our line was **[+ pres_runoff_endorsement +]**, and
the last fortnight was spent on **[+ pres_runoff_final_push +]**; no campaign
will ever know what the other version of it would have produced.

- @runoff_consequences: Record the political consequences

@runoff_consequences
title: A presidency and a party system
new-page: true

[? if pres_runoff_winner_key = "duda": Duda remains in the Palace, but the
campaign has tested how far he can act as PiS's candidate and how far he can
build a mandate of his own.?]

[? if pres_runoff_winner_key = "trzaskowski": Poland enters cohabitation: a KO
candidate has won the count, but PiS still controls the institutions that must
certify the result, convene the National Assembly and hear the oath.?]

[? if pres_runoff_winner_key = "kidawa": Poland enters cohabitation behind the
candidate KO spent the spring trying to replace. She has won the count; PiS
still controls the institutions that must certify the result, convene the
National Assembly and hear the oath, and her own party now has to govern the
Palace it did not want her in.?]

[? if pres_runoff_winner_key = "left": The almost impossible route has opened.
The Left holds the presidency without controlling the government, and every
faction now claims ownership of the victory.?]

[? if pres_runoff_winner_key = "holownia": Hołownia reaches the Palace before
building a party. His volunteer campaign becomes an immediate centrist pole.?]

[? if pres_runoff_winner_key = "kosiniak": PSL has achieved a national prize
far beyond its parliamentary size. Every coalition will pay for it.?]

[? if pres_runoff_winner_key = "bosak": A radical-right presidency breaks the
old democratic-camp arithmetic and accelerates the struggle inside
Konfederacja.?]

- @runoff_consequences_continue

@runoff_consequences_continue
title: Return to the post-election campaign
go-to: poland_kwasniewski.presidential_victory if pres_runoff_winner_key = "left" and kwasniewski_estranged = 0 and kwasniewski_alignment >= 40 and kwasniewski_presidential_payoff_year != 2020; poland_hub

@challenger_inauguration_2020
# prose-audit: Grade A — The distinction between election and accession is now dramatised rather than asserted: the Assembly convenes on screen, the outgoing President is present, and the powers change hands in a named sequence before office incompatibility is routed onward.
title: The President-elect takes the oath
face-image: img/poland/events/presidential-palace.webp
new-page: true
on-arrival: {!
Q.pres_generic_inauguration_done = 1;
Q.president_name = Q.pres_2020_president_elect_name ||
    Q.pres_runoff_winner_name;
Q.left_president =
    Q.pres_2020_president_elect_key == "left" ? 1 : 0;
Q.pres_2020_phase = "Presidency active";
Q.news_headline = Q.president_name +
    " takes office after the constitutional oath";
!}

= 6 August 2020 — Election is not inauguration

For eleven weeks the country has had a President and a President-elect at the
same time, and only one of them has been able to sign anything. Andrzej Duda
remains head of state until the moment the oath is finished — not until the
count, not until the Supreme Court's validation, not until the concession.

The National Assembly convenes at ten. Both chambers sit together in the Sejm
chamber; the outgoing President is in the second row, which is the part of the
ceremony nobody rehearses well. The Marshal reads the validation resolution.
**[+ president_name +]** stands, delivers the constitutional formula, and adds
the optional religious ending or does not — the one line of the morning that is
genuinely a choice.

Then the powers move, all at once and in a fixed order: the veto, the
appointments, the ratifications, the command of the armed forces, the nuclear
briefcase's less dramatic Polish equivalent. Somebody hands over the seal of
the Order of the White Eagle. By eleven the Palace has a different tenant and
an unchanged staff, most of whom will be replaced by October.

Any parliamentary or party office the new President was holding an hour ago is
now vacant by operation of law, and must pass to its lawful successor before
anybody has finished lunch.

- @challenger_inauguration_record

@challenger_inauguration_record
title: Record the oath and resolve any resulting vacancy
call: poland_normalize
go-to: poland_office_authority.resolve if office_incompatibility_pending = 1; poland_hub if office_incompatibility_pending = 0
